// Longer rules summaries, paraphrased from https://dnd5e.wikidot.com (CC BY-SA 3.0). Generated; see README.
window.DND = window.DND || {};
DND.spellText = {"Blade Ward":"Blade Ward is a one-action abjuration cantrip that targets only you. Until the end of your next turn, weapon strikes that deal bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage do less harm to you.",
"Resistance":"This touch-range cantrip lets a willing creature add a d4 to one saving throw of its choice, rolled before or after the save. It works once and lasts up to a minute while concentration holds, then ends. It involves no attack, area, or damage, and no higher-level scaling is listed.",
"Virtue (UA)":"This abjuration cantrip lets you touch a creature with at least 1 hit point, granting temporary hit points equal to a d4 roll plus your spellcasting modifier.",
"Absorb Elements":"Triggered by taking acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage, this reaction spell gives you resistance to that type until your next turn begins. Your next melee hit then deals an extra 1d6 of that damage and ends the spell. Each spell slot level above 1st adds another 1d6.",
"Alarm":"This 1st-level ritual guards a door, window, or area up to a 20-foot cube within 30 feet for 8 hours. It causes no damage and has no saving throw. When a creature Tiny or larger enters, the caster gets a mental ping or a bell-like sound. No higher-level scaling is given.",
"Armor of Agathys":"You gain 5 temporary hit points for an hour, and any creature that lands a melee hit on you takes 5 cold damage. Casting it with a higher-level slot adds 5 more temporary hit points and 5 more cold damage for each slot level above first.",
"Ceremony":"Ceremony is a 1st-level ritual that takes an hour and consumes 25 gp of powdered silver. The caster picks one of six rites on a touched target within 10 feet, such as restoring a willing creature's alignment, blessing water, or giving a d4 bonus to checks or saves.",
"Mage Armor":"Mage Armor enchants a willing creature you touch that wears no armor, setting its base AC at 13 plus its Dexterity modifier. The effect lasts 8 hours but ends early if the target puts on armor or you dismiss it as an action.",
"Protection from Evil and Good":"This 1st-level abjuration gives a willing creature you touch defense against aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, fiends, and undead for up to 10 minutes of concentration. Those creatures attack it at disadvantage and cannot charm, frighten, or possess it. No damage, saving throw, area, or higher-level scaling is listed.",
"Sanctuary":"Costing a bonus action, this 1st-level abjuration guards one creature within 30 feet for a minute. Attackers and harmful spellcasters must pass a Wisdom save or redirect elsewhere. Area effects still hit the warded creature, and the ward ends if it attacks, casts an offensive spell, or harms another creature.",
"Shield":"When an attack is about to hit you or a magic missile targets you, you raise a force barrier that adds 5 to your AC, including against the triggering attack, until your next turn begins. It also blocks all damage from that magic missile.",
"Shield of Faith":"Wraps a chosen creature in a glimmering shield that raises its Armor Class by 2. You must keep concentrating on it, and it can last up to ten minutes.",
"Snare":"Creates a hard-to-spot 5-foot magic trap that snares Small to Large creatures stepping into it, forcing a Dexterity save or hoisting them upside down 3 feet off the ground. Victims can retry that save each turn, or a nearby creature can free them with an Arcana check against your spell save DC.",
"Aid":"Up to three chosen allies each gain 5 extra hit points, raising both their maximum and current totals. Casting it with a slot above second level adds 5 more hit points per level beyond second for each target.",
"Arcane Lock":"Seals a closed door, chest, or similar opening so nothing can pass it, except creatures the caster chooses, until the effect is dispelled. A spoken passphrase can suppress it for one minute, and Knock can suppress it for ten. Breaking the item or picking its lock becomes ten points harder.",
"Digital Phantom (UA)":"While concentrating for up to an hour, you and chosen network users gain +10 to Intelligence checks to avoid detection by monitors and tracking programs. Whenever you leave a system, all evidence of your earlier presence there is wiped out.",
"Lesser Restoration":"By touching a creature, you can rid it of one illness or one of four ailments: blindness, deafness, paralysis, or poisoning.",
"Mental Barrier (UA)":"When a mental-based save (Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma) is forced on you, you can respond by shielding your thoughts. Until your next turn begins, those saves are made with advantage, and you take half damage from psychic harm.",
"Pass without Trace":"Chosen creatures within 30 feet, including the caster, gain a +10 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) checks. They can be tracked only by magic and leave no trail while moving.",
"Protection from Poison":"One touched creature has a single poison ended, chosen from a known one if several afflict it. For the next hour, that creature has advantage on saves against becoming poisoned and resists poison damage.",
"Thought Shield (UA)":"Touching a creature hides its thoughts for eight hours, blocking mind-reading, detection, and telepathic contact unless the creature allows it. The creature also gains advantage on saves against effects that check whether it is lying.",
"Warding Bond":"A willing ally you touch gains a +1 bonus to Armor Class and saving throws, plus resistance to all damage, while within 60 feet of you. Each bit of harm they take is mirrored onto you, and the link breaks if you fall unconscious or the two of you drift too far apart.",
"Beacon of Hope":"While you concentrate for up to a minute, chosen allies roll Wisdom and death saving throws with an edge. Any healing they receive also restores the maximum possible amount.",
"Counterspell":"Interrupts a spell as another creature is casting it, automatically stopping spells of 3rd level or lower. Against higher-level spells, you roll a spellcasting ability check against DC 10 plus the spell's level. Casting it with a higher-level slot automatically stops spells up to that slot's level.",
"Dispel Magic":"Automatically ends any spell of 3rd level or lower on a chosen creature, object, or magical effect. Higher-level spells instead require a spellcasting ability check against DC 10 plus their level, ending them on success. Using a higher slot automatically ends spells up to that slot's level.",
"Glyph of Warding":"Creates a hidden trap on a surface or container that fires when a chosen trigger occurs. It either bursts in a 20-foot radius, where creatures make a Dexterity save for 5d8 damage of a chosen type (half on success), or releases a stored spell. Higher slots add 1d8 per level beyond 3rd to the burst.",
"Intellect Fortress":"While you maintain focus for up to an hour, you or one willing creature you can see gains defense against psychic harm and an edge on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saves. Casting it with a higher slot lets you affect one extra creature per level above third, all within 30 feet of each other.",
"Magic Circle":"Builds a 10-foot-wide, 20-foot-tall barrier lasting an hour that keeps chosen creature types like fiends or undead out unless they pass a Charisma save to teleport in. Those creatures attack at disadvantage against anyone inside, and anyone inside is shielded from their charm, fear, or possession. Each slot level above 3rd adds an hour.",
"Nondetection":"For eight hours, you conceal a touched willing creature, or a place or object up to 10 feet in any dimension, from divination spells and magical scrying sensors. Such magic cannot be aimed at it to find it.",
"Protection from Ballistics (UA)":"Shields a creature's body against ordinary bullets and similar projectiles, so non-magical ballistic harm deals only half its normal damage. The protection lasts while you maintain concentration, for up to ten minutes.",
"Protection from Energy":"Chosen on touch, a willing ally takes only half damage from one element you select: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder. The protection lasts as long as you keep concentrating on it.",
"Remove Curse":"Dissolves every curse afflicting one creature or object. If the target is a cursed magic item, the curse lingers, but the owner's bond to the item is broken so it can be discarded.",
"Aura of Life":"Creates a moving 30-foot-radius field around you that lasts up to 10 minutes while you concentrate. Non-hostile creatures inside gain protection from necrotic harm and can't have their maximum hit points lowered. A living one knocked to 0 hit points regains 1 hit point at the start of its turn.",
"Aura of Purity":"Creatures that aren't hostile to the caster, including the caster, within a 30-foot aura that travels with them are immune to disease and resist poison damage. They also roll saves against seven named conditions with advantage.",
"Banishment":"Forces one visible creature to make a Charisma save or be sent away. Creatures from your plane are shunted into a harmless pocket dimension where they're incapacitated until the effect ends, while outsiders are sent back to their home plane. Casting it with a 5th-level or higher slot adds one more target per level above 4th.",
"Death Ward":"This spell guards a touched creature against death. The first time damage would reduce it to zero hit points, it stays conscious at 1 hit point instead, and the magic fades. It also blocks one instant-death effect that deals no damage, which ends the spell as well.",
"Freedom of Movement":"For an hour, one willing creature ignores difficult terrain and can't be slowed, paralyzed, or immobilized by magic. Spending 5 feet of movement lets it slip free of ordinary shackles or grapples, and water imposes no penalties on its movement or attacks.",
"Gate Seal":"Creates a stationary 30-foot cube where portals are sealed and planar travel fails, including gate and plane shift, for 24 hours. Using a 6th-level or higher slot removes the time limit, so it persists until dispelled.",
"Mordenkainen's Private Sanctum":"Creates a protected cube up to 100 feet per side that lasts 24 hours unless you dismiss it. You choose which protections apply: blocking sound, sight (including darkvision), divination sensors and targeting, teleportation, and planar travel. Each spell slot level above 4th adds 100 feet to the cube's size.",
"Stoneskin":"Touching a willing ally hardens their skin like stone, halving damage from ordinary blows, bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing, that isn't magical. The effect lasts up to an hour while you keep concentrating.",
"Antilife Shell":"Creates a mobile barrier, 10-foot radius, that follows you and keeps out every creature except undead and constructs, stopping them from walking or reaching through. Affected creatures can still cast spells or strike with ranged or reach weapons across it, and the effect ends if you push one through.",
"Banishing Smite":"Your next weapon hit while you maintain concentration adds 5d10 force damage. If that hit leaves the target at 50 hit points or fewer, it's banished: creatures from other planes return home, while others are trapped, incapacitated, in a harmless pocket realm until the spell ends.",
"Circle of Power":"Creates a 30-foot sphere around you that follows your movement for up to ten minutes while you concentrate. Friendly creatures inside, including you, make saving throws against spells and magic with advantage, and a successful save against a half-damage effect negates the damage entirely.",
"Dispel Evil and Good":"While it lasts, celestials, elementals, fey, fiends, and undead attack you at disadvantage. Ending it early lets you free a charmed or frightened creature with a touch, or make a melee spell attack that forces a Charisma save, sending the target back to its home plane.",
"Greater Restoration":"Touching a creature, this magic can lower its exhaustion by one level or clear one lasting harm: a charm or petrification, a curse (including a bond to a cursed item), a drained ability score, or a reduced hit point maximum.",
"Planar Binding":"Forces a celestial, elemental, fey, or fiend to make a Charisma save, and on a failure it obeys you for 24 hours. Using higher slots stretches that to anywhere from 10 days to just over a year.",
"Druid Grove":"Calling on nature spirits, this ward covers an outdoor or underground cube 30 to 90 feet per side, leaving structures out. Inside, you can create dense fog, grasping vines, up to four animated trees that guard the area, and one wind or thorn effect. Chosen friends or a spoken passphrase grant immunity.",
"Fizban's Platinum Shield":"Shrouds a chosen creature, possibly the caster, in silver light that grants half cover and resistance to five elemental and poison damage types. Against Dexterity saves for half damage, a success negates the damage and a failure halves it. Later, a bonus action can move the light to another creature within 60 feet of it.",
"Forbiddance":"Creates a day-long ward over a large area that blocks teleportation, portal entry, and planar travel. Chosen creature types take 5d10 radiant or necrotic damage (the caster's choice) when they enter or start a turn inside, unless they speak a password set at casting.",
"Globe of Invulnerability":"Creates a stationary, shimmering shield with a 10-foot radius around the caster. Spells of 5th level or lower cast from outside can target creatures or objects inside but have no effect there. Each slot level above 6th raises the blocked spell level by one.",
"Guards and Wards":"Lasting a full day, this ritual shields a region of about 2,500 square feet, up to 20 feet tall. Fog fills corridors and may misdirect travelers at forks, doors lock and can be disguised as walls, stairs get choked with webbing, and one extra magical trick is added.",
"Primordial Ward":"Shields you against five elemental damage types, halving harm from them. When one of those types strikes you, you can react to become immune to it, including that very hit, and the spell ends at the close of your next turn.",
"Symbol":"Hidden on a surface or inside a container, this ward activates when its chosen trigger occurs and lights a 60-foot-radius area for 10 minutes. Creatures there must make a saving throw against the selected effect. The Death option deals 10d10 necrotic damage, halved on a successful Constitution save.",
"Antimagic Field":"Creates a moving bubble around the caster that cancels magic inside it. Spells and magic items stop working, magic aimed at targets inside fails, summoned beings vanish, and teleportation is blocked. Lasts up to an hour while concentrating.",
"Holy Aura":"Creates a 30-foot radiant aura around you. Chosen allies in it shed dim light and gain advantage on saving throws, while other creatures attacking them roll with disadvantage. When a fiend or undead melee-hits a protected ally, the attacker makes a Constitution save or is blinded for the duration.",
"Mind Blank":"A willing creature you touch becomes shielded from mental harm, including psychic damage, being charmed, and attempts to sense feelings or read thoughts, and divination magic is blocked too. Even wish-level magic aimed at their mind or at learning about them fails.",
"Imprisonment":"A visible creature must pass a Wisdom save or be imprisoned in one of five forms you choose: buried underground, chained in place, sealed in a tiny pocket realm, shrunk inside a gem, or put into endless sleep. Success grants immunity to later casts. Lasts until dispelled or a release condition you set occurs.",
"Invulnerability":"For up to ten minutes, as long as you keep concentrating, you cannot be harmed by any kind of damage.",
"Prismatic Wall":"Creatures pushing through its seven colored layers make a Dexterity save for each one. Red, orange, yellow, green, and blue deal 10d6 damage (half on a success), while indigo can restrain and petrify and violet can banish.",
"Acid Splash":"Choose one visible creature, or two creatures within 5 feet of each other, and hurl an acid bubble at them. Each target makes a Dexterity save or takes 1d6 acid damage. The damage rises to 2d6, 3d6, and then 4d6 as the caster reaches higher levels.",
"Create Bonfire":"A conjured fire fills a 5-foot cube on visible ground for up to a minute while you concentrate. Creatures inside it, or entering or ending their turn there, make a Dexterity save or take 1d8 fire damage, gaining an extra 1d8 at levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Infestation":"A creature you can see must pass a Constitution save or take 1d6 poison damage and be nudged 5 feet in a random cardinal direction, without provoking opportunity attacks. It stays put if that direction is blocked. The damage rises to 2d6, 3d6, and 4d6 at 5th, 11th, and 17th level.",
"Mage Hand":"You conjure a spectral hand that you direct with your action to handle objects, open unlocked doors or containers, and shift up to 30 feet each use. It can't attack, trigger magic items, or carry more than 10 pounds.",
"Poison Spray":"A creature you can see must fail a Constitution save or take 1d12 poison damage from a burst of poisonous vapor. The damage rises as you gain levels, to 2d12 at 5th, 3d12 at 11th, and 4d12 at 17th.",
"Produce Flame":"A harmless flame lingers in your hand, lighting a 10-foot radius plus dim light beyond it. Throw it at a foe within 30 feet with a ranged spell attack to deal 1d8 fire damage on a hit, which ends the effect. Damage gains an extra 1d8 at levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Sword Burst":"Spectral blades whirl outward to strike every creature within 5 feet of you. Each one that fails a Dexterity save takes 1d6 force damage, which grows to 2d6, 3d6, and 4d6 at higher character levels.",
"Arms of Hadar":"Dark tendrils lash every creature within a 10-foot circle around you, and each must resist with a Strength save. Those who fail take 2d6 necrotic damage and lose reactions until their next turn. Success halves the damage with no further consequence. Higher-level casting adds 1d6 damage per level beyond first.",
"Ensnaring Strike":"Your next weapon hit makes thorny vines erupt, and the target must pass a Strength save or stay restrained. Large or bigger foes have advantage on that save. Restrained targets take 1d6 piercing damage each turn and can break free with a Strength check against your save DC. Each slot above first adds 1d6 damage.",
"Entangle":"Grasping plants erupt across a 20-foot square, making the ground difficult terrain for up to a minute while concentration lasts. Creatures inside must succeed on a Strength save or be held fast, but they can spend an action on a Strength check against the caster's save DC to break free.",
"Find Familiar":"Summons a spirit companion in one of several animal forms. It acts on its own in combat, obeys your orders, and can't attack. You can talk to it telepathically within 100 feet, see through its senses, and have it deliver touch-range spells for you.",
"Fog Cloud":"Creates a fog sphere roughly 20 feet in radius that wraps around corners and leaves everything inside heavily obscured. It lasts up to an hour while you concentrate, unless a moderate wind of 10 mph or more blows it away. Each spell slot level above 1st adds 20 feet to the radius.",
"Grease":"Covers a 10-foot square with slippery residue that counts as difficult terrain. Creatures inside when it appears, or who enter it or end a turn there, must make a Dexterity save or fall prone.",
"Hail of Thorns":"Your next ranged weapon hit, made within the next minute, releases thorns from your weapon or ammunition. The target and creatures within 5 feet must each make a Dexterity save, taking 1d10 piercing damage on a failure or half on a success. Each spell slot level above 1st adds 1d10, to a maximum of 6d10.",
"Healing Elixir (UA)":"Creates a healing potion in a vial that stays usable for a day or until someone uses it, and the vial vanishes once it's consumed. Using it takes an action, and the drinker, either you or another creature, recovers 2d4 + 2 hit points.",
"Ice Knife":"Launch an icy shard at one foe with a ranged spell attack, dealing 1d10 piercing on a hit. The shard then bursts, and the target plus creatures within 5 feet must make a Dexterity save or take 2d6 cold damage. Each slot level above first adds 1d6 cold damage.",
"Tenser's Floating Disk":"Creates a flat, floating force platform about three feet across, hovering three feet off the ground and holding up to 500 pounds for an hour. It drifts along to stay within 20 feet of you, but it collapses if overloaded or if you wander more than 100 feet away.",
"Unseen Servant":"Summons an unseen, mindless helper with 1 hit point and no attack ability for chores like fetching, cleaning, or serving. Each turn, a bonus action moves it up to 15 feet to perform one task, and it ends if destroyed or sent over 60 feet away.",
"Air Bubble":"Encloses a willing creature's head in a spectral sphere of breathable air that lasts until the spell ends. If the creature has several heads, the sphere forms around only one. Each spell slot level above 2nd adds two more air globes.",
"Cloud of Daggers":"Whirling blades fill a five-foot cube at a point you pick, and any creature that enters that space or starts its turn there takes 4d4 slashing harm. Each spell slot above second level adds 2d4 damage.",
"Dust Devil":"Conjure a whirling dust devil in a visible 5-foot cube that you can drift 30 feet as a bonus action. Creatures ending turns within 5 feet make a Strength save, taking 1d8 bludgeoning damage and being shoved 10 feet on a failure, or half damage on success. Each slot level above second adds 1d8.",
"Find Steed":"This spell summons a loyal, unusually sharp steed, shaped like a horse, camel, or mastiff, that you can ride and speak with telepathically within a mile. While you're mounted, your self-targeted spells can also affect the steed.",
"Find Vehicle (UA)":"Summons a nonmilitary land vehicle of celestial, fey, or fiendish origin, which you can drive with proficiency and double your proficiency bonus on driving checks. Higher-level slots allow a water vehicle (3rd), an air vehicle (5th), or any vehicle with DM approval (7th).",
"Flaming Sphere":"A mobile ball of flame that burns creatures ending their turn within 5 feet, who make a Dexterity save: 2d6 fire damage on a failure, half on a success. A bonus action lets you steer it up to 30 feet, and ramming a foe forces the same save. Casting with a higher slot adds 1d6 damage per level above 2nd.",
"Flock of Familiars":"Summons three spirit companions in animal forms, all of one kind: celestial, fey, or fiend. They share senses and chat telepathically with you within a mile, and you can deliver one touch spell per turn through them. Using a higher slot adds one more companion for each level above second.",
"Healing Spirit":"A nature spirit occupies a 5-foot cube you choose and restores 1d6 hit points to anyone who enters or starts a turn there, skipping constructs and undead. You can shift it up to 30 feet, and it vanishes after healing a number of times equal to 1 plus your spellcasting modifier (minimum two). Each slot level above second adds another 1d6.",
"Misty Step":"In an instant, you blink yourself up to 30 feet to any empty spot within your line of sight, wrapped in a brief shimmer of haze.",
"Spray of Cards":"Summoning a fan of ghostly playing cards across a 15-foot cone, this spell makes each creature inside attempt a Dexterity save. Failing deals 2d10 force damage and blinds the target until its next turn ends, while succeeding halves the damage. Higher slots add 1d10 damage per level beyond second.",
"Summon Beast":"Summons a loyal animal spirit shaped by a chosen habitat, which acts right after you. Its melee strike uses your spell attack bonus, dealing 1d8 + 4 plus the spell's level in piercing damage. More attacks come at higher levels, and its 20 or 30 hit points rise by 5 per level above 2nd.",
"Vortex Warp":"Forces a visible creature to make a Constitution save, though it may choose to fail. On a failure, you shift it to a spot you select within sight that can bear its weight. Each slot level above 2nd extends the reach by 30 feet.",
"Web":"Fills a 20-foot cube with sticky webbing that lasts while you concentrate, up to an hour. Creatures that start a turn in it or enter it must make a Dexterity save or become restrained, and they can break free with a Strength check against your save DC. Burning webs deal 2d4 fire damage to creatures in the flames.",
"Wristpocket":"Hide a small item you're holding, weighing 5 pounds or less, in a pocket dimension for up to an hour while you maintain focus. Spend an action to pull it back into your free hand or stash it again. If the spell ends while it's stored, it reappears at your feet.",
"Call Lightning":"Summon a storm cloud, then each turn hurl lightning at a visible spot beneath it. Creatures within 5 feet of that spot make a Dexterity save, taking 3d10 lightning damage on a failure or half on success. Damage rises by 1d10 per slot level above 3rd, and by 1d10 when cast amid outdoor storms.",
"Conjure Animals":"Summons fey beasts into empty visible spaces: one of CR 2 or lower, two of CR 1 or lower, four of CR 1/2 or lower, or eight of CR 1/4 or lower. They obey orders and vanish at 0 hit points. Higher slots double, triple, or quadruple the count at 5th, 7th, and 9th.",
"Conjure Barrage":"Launch a plain weapon or piece of ammunition to create a spray of identical missiles across a 60-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save, taking 3d8 damage of the weapon's type on a failure or half on a success.",
"Conjure Lesser Demon (UA)":"Summons up to eight hostile lesser fiends, rising to sixteen or thirty-two with higher-level slots. They attack the nearest non-fiends until slain or the spell ends. A blood ring drawn on the ground keeps them from crossing it or harming anyone inside.",
"Create Food and Water":"Conjures about 45 pounds of plain but filling food and 30 gallons of pure water on the ground or in containers nearby. The supply feeds up to fifteen people or five mounts for a full day. Leftover food spoils after that day, but the water never goes bad.",
"Galder's Tower":"Conjures a sturdy two-story tower, up to 100 square feet per floor, that lasts a day and stays warm and dry inside. You choose each floor's furnished or empty layout, and casting it with a higher slot adds one floor per slot level above 3rd.",
"House of Cards (UA)":"Over 24 hours, you raise a three-floor tower of giant playing cards on a 30-foot square base, giving occupants half cover. Each card has AC 10 and 1 hit point, and whenever one is destroyed, you roll a d6, with a 5 or 6 collapsing the whole structure.",
"Hunger of Hadar":"Conjures a 20-foot sphere of freezing darkness at a chosen point, blinding creatures fully inside and making the space difficult terrain. Creatures starting their turn there take 2d6 cold damage, and those ending a turn there must make a Dexterity save or take 2d6 acid damage.",
"Sleet Storm":"Icy rain fills a 40-foot-radius column, heavily obscuring vision and dousing open flames while leaving the ground slick. Creatures entering or starting a turn there must succeed on a Dexterity save or fall prone, and concentrating casters must pass a Constitution save or lose focus.",
"Spirit Guardians":"Spirits surround you in a 15-foot radius for up to ten minutes while you concentrate, halving enemies' speed there; chosen allies are exempt. Creatures entering or starting a turn there make a Wisdom save, taking 3d8 radiant or necrotic damage on a failure and half on a success. Each slot level above third adds 1d8 damage.",
"Stinking Cloud":"A 20-foot-radius cloud of nauseating gas appears at a chosen spot and lasts up to a minute while you concentrate, heavily obscuring its area. Creatures inside at the start of their turn make a Constitution save against poison, and on a failure they lose their action to gagging and stumbling. Winds of 10 mph or more eventually clear it, and stronger gusts do so faster.",
"Summon Fey":"A summoned fey spirit with 30 hit points (plus 10 per level above 3rd) strikes for 1d6 + 3 + spell level piercing plus 1d6 force. Its bonus-action mood can charm a nearby foe on a failed Wisdom save, or cloak a 5-foot cube in darkness.",
"Summon Lesser Demons":"Two, four, or eight fiends appear, depending on a d6 roll, with challenge ratings capped at 1, 1/2, or 1/4 respectively, and they turn on everyone, caster included. A blood ring bars them from crossing, harming, or targeting anyone inside. A 6th or 7th-level slot doubles the count; 8th or 9th triples it.",
"Summon Shadowspawn":"Summons a shadowy ally that acts right after you and obeys spoken orders. Its chilling hand makes a spell attack for 1d12+3 plus cold damage, and a once-daily scream forces foes within 30 feet to make Wisdom saves or become frightened. Higher-level casts boost its hit points, attacks, and damage.",
"Summon Warrior Spirit (UA)":"Summons a spirit styled as a barbarian, fighter, or monk that you can command for up to an hour while concentrating, acting right after your turn. Its strikes deal 1d12, 1d6, or 1d4 plus 3 and the spell's level, and it has 30 HP (20 for the monk) plus 10 per level above 3rd.",
"Thunder Step":"You vanish to a visible, open spot and leave a booming blast behind. Creatures within 10 feet of where you stood make a Constitution save, taking 3d10 thunder damage on a failure or half on a success. Damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level used above the base.",
"Tidal Wave":"Summoning a crashing wave across a 30-foot-long, 10-foot-wide, 10-foot-tall area, this spell forces Dexterity saves. Failing deals 4d8 bludgeoning damage and knocks targets prone, while succeeding halves the damage and avoids the fall.",
"Conjure Barlgura (UA)":"Calls forth a demonic beast that acts on its own turns, charging the nearest non-demon it can sense and wandering randomly if no foes are visible. A blood-drawn circle can bar it from crossing or striking anyone inside. It disappears at zero hit points or when the effect ends, lasting up to ten minutes.",
"Conjure Knowbot (UA)":"For 10 minutes, a touched computer hosts a semi-aware software helper that, on your bonus action, handles digital tasks normally needing an action, rolling Intelligence checks. Slots of 5th level or higher stretch it to an hour, extend your link to 1,000 feet, and let it finish its last order if you wander off.",
"Conjure Minor Elementals":"Summons a group of friendly elementals into empty visible spaces nearby. You pick one strong, two medium, four weak, or eight very weak creatures. They follow spoken orders and vanish at 0 hit points or when your focus ends. Using a 6th- or 8th-level slot doubles or triples the number summoned.",
"Conjure Shadow Demon (UA)":"Summons a demon that acts on its own turns and follows your orders while it keeps attacking a foe each turn and stays out of bright light. If it stops, a contested Charisma check can free it from your control. A blood circle keeps it from crossing or targeting anyone inside.",
"Conjure Woodland Beings":"Summons a group of friendly fey creatures, with your choice of one of CR 2 or lower, two of CR 1 or lower, four of CR 1/2 or lower, or eight of CR 1/4 or lower. They follow your spoken orders and vanish when slain or when concentration ends. Higher-level slots multiply the number summoned.",
"Dimension Door":"Lets you relocate yourself to a spot you can see, imagine, or define by direction and distance, optionally taking one willing nearby companion and your portable gear. Arriving in an occupied space deals 4d6 force damage to you and your companion, and the teleport fails.",
"Evard's Black Tentacles":"Dark, writhing tentacles cover a 20-foot patch of ground, making it difficult terrain. Creatures that enter or begin their turn there must pass a Dexterity save or take 3d6 bludgeoning damage and become trapped, then take 3d6 more each turn they stay caught. Trapped creatures escape with a Strength or Dexterity check versus your save DC.",
"Find Greater Steed":"A loyal spirit takes the form of a mount you pick, like a griffon, dire wolf, or rhinoceros, using its standard monster stats. You command it in battle and speak to it telepathically within a mile. It vanishes at 0 HP and returns fully healed when you recast, and only one bond is allowed.",
"Galder's Speedy Courier":"Summons a nearly transparent air elemental carrying a three-foot chest that you stuff with items, then delivers it to a creature you know or have a body part of. Only the recipient can open it for up to ten minutes, after which leftovers drop at your feet. Using an 8th-level slot lets it reach other planes.",
"Grasping Vine":"A vine sprouts where you choose and can snap at a visible creature in its reach, hauling a failed target twenty feet closer unless they resist with nimble footwork. While you keep concentration, you can lash again with a bonus action on each of your turns.",
"Guardian of Faith":"A spectral guardian takes up a space you can see and attacks hostile creatures that first enter within 10 feet of it on their turn. Those creatures make a Dexterity save, taking 20 radiant damage on a failure or half on a success. The guardian vanishes after it has dealt 60 total damage.",
"Leomund's Secret Chest":"You hide a chest and its nonliving contents in the Ethereal Plane, up to 12 cubic feet. You can summon it to an open spot beside you or send it back by touching both it and its miniature twin. After 60 days, the magic may fade with a growing daily chance, permanently losing anything still stored away.",
"Mordenkainen's Faithful Hound":"A phantom watchdog that only you can perceive guards a spot for up to 8 hours, barking at intruders who lack your password. Each of your turns, it bites one hostile creature within 5 feet, making an attack roll with your spellcasting modifier plus proficiency and dealing 4d8 piercing damage on a hit.",
"Summon Aberration":"Summons an aberrant ally that acts right after you and obeys spoken commands, dodging if left idle. Its attacks deal 1d8 or 1d10, plus 3 and the spell's level, while a Star Spawn's aura forces Wisdom saves for 2d6 psychic damage within 5 feet. Higher slots add hit points and attacks.",
"Summon Construct":"Summons a construct ally with 40 hit points, plus 15 for each spell level above 4th. Its spell-attack slam deals 1d8+4 plus the spell's level in bludgeoning damage. It makes attacks equal to half the spell's level and vanishes at 0 hit points or when concentration ends.",
"Summon Elemental":"Summons a Medium elemental ally that makes melee slam attacks using your spell attack bonus, dealing 1d10, plus 4, plus the spell's level in damage. It gets one attack per two spell levels and has 50 hit points, plus 10 for each level above fourth.",
"Summon Greater Demon":"Summons a demon of challenge rating 5 or less that follows your spoken orders, but it makes a Charisma save at the end of each of its turns to break free. Speaking its true name gives that save disadvantage. Each slot level above fourth raises the maximum challenge rating by one.",
"Watery Sphere":"Creatures in a 5-foot-radius water sphere must pass a Strength save or become trapped inside, retrying at the end of each turn; passing ejects them instead. The sphere holds up to four Medium creatures or one Large, and you can drag it up to 30 feet per action.",
"Cloudkill":"Summons a 20-foot-radius cloud of toxic fog that blocks sight and drifts 10 feet away from the caster each turn. Creatures that enter it or begin their turn inside must make a Constitution save, taking 5d8 poison damage on a failure or half on a success. Each spell slot level above 5th adds 1d8 damage.",
"Conjure Elemental":"Summons an elemental with challenge rating 5 or lower that matches a chosen air, earth, fire, or water 10-foot cube and obeys your spoken commands while you concentrate. If concentration breaks, it turns hostile instead. Higher slots raise the maximum challenge rating by one per slot level above the base.",
"Conjure Volley":"Duplicates of a fired or thrown nonmagical weapon rain down on a chosen spot. Creatures within a 40-foot-wide, 20-foot-tall cylinder there make a Dexterity save, taking 8d8 damage of the weapon's type on a failure or half on a success.",
"Conjure Vrock (UA)":"Summons a demonic vrock that obeys you only while you pass hidden Charisma checks. The DC starts at 10 and rises by 2 each round, and a bonus equal to the gem's value divided by 20 helps. Failing frees the vrock to seek treasure, and an optional blood circle can keep it from entering your space.",
"Far Step":"Requiring concentration for up to a minute, this lets you instantly jump to any empty spot you can see within 60 feet. You can keep making these short leaps on later turns while it lasts.",
"Infernal Calling":"Summon a devil of challenge rating 6 or lower that acts on its own, possibly attacking you or tempting you toward evil. Issue it commands through a contested Charisma check against its Wisdom (Insight), with an edge if you use its true name. Each spell slot above 5th raises the devil's challenge rating by one.",
"Insect Plague":"Conjures a 20-foot-radius swarm of biting insects that deals 4d10 piercing damage to creatures in it, or half on a successful Constitution save. Creatures must save again when they enter the swarm or end a turn inside it. Each spell slot above 5th adds 1d10 damage.",
"Steel Wind Strike":"Up to five visible creatures each face a melee spell attack, and every hit deals 6d10 force damage. Afterward, the caster can relocate to an open space beside any one of those targets, whether the attack landed or not.",
"Summon Celestial":"Summons an angelic ally that attacks with a radiant bow for 2d6+2 plus the spell's level, or a radiant mace for 1d10+3 plus the spell's level. Its 40 hit points grow by 10 per spell level above fifth, and once a day it heals a creature for 2d8 plus the spell's level.",
"Summon Draconic Spirit":"Summons a large dragon ally with 50 hit points that acts right after you. Its melee spell attacks deal 1d6+4 plus the spell's level in piercing damage, and its 30-foot cone breath forces Dexterity saves for 2d6 damage, halved on success. Each spell level above 5th adds 10 hit points and strengthens its attacks.",
"Teleportation Circle":"Sketch a 10-foot ring of sigils to open a portal linked to a known permanent circle on the same plane. Creatures stepping through appear near that destination, and the gateway closes when your next turn ends.",
"Tree Stride":"Lets you slip into a living tree and emerge from another matching tree up to 500 feet away, spending movement to do so. While it lasts, you sense every similar tree in that range, can travel between them once each round, and must end each turn standing outside a tree.",
"Arcane Gate":"Lasting up to ten minutes while you concentrate, this links two 10-foot rings set near the ground so anything stepping into one comes out of the other. Their misty surfaces block sight, and you can spin them to choose which side is active.",
"Conjure Fey":"Summons a fey creature of challenge rating 6 or lower, or a beast-shaped fey spirit, that acts on its own turns and obeys your spoken commands while you concentrate for up to an hour. Losing concentration turns it hostile. Each higher slot level adds 1 to the maximum challenge rating.",
"Drawmij's Instant Summons":"Mark a small object (10 lb or less), then later use an action to speak its name and crush the linked gem, instantly pulling the item to your hand from any distance. If a creature holds it, you instead learn its identity and rough location. Dispel magic on the gem ends it.",
"Heroes' Feast":"Conjures a lavish banquet for up to twelve creatures, who need an hour to finish it. Afterward, each diner sheds diseases and poison, becomes immune to poison and fear, and rolls Wisdom saves with advantage. Each also gains 2d10 extra maximum and current hit points for a day.",
"Planar Ally":"Calling on a deity or other cosmic power you know, you summon a celestial, elemental, or fiend into an open space nearby. It acts on its own terms, so you must bargain for its help with gold, magic items, sacrifices, or quests, with costs rising the longer the task takes.",
"Scatter":"Up to five visible creatures are shunted to empty spots you can see around you, and unwilling targets can avoid it with a Wisdom save. Landing spots must be solid ground or a floor.",
"Summon Fiend":"Conjure a demon, devil, or yugoloth ally that lasts up to an hour. Its bite, claws, or fire bolt deal 1d12, 1d8, or 2d6 damage plus the spell's level, and a demon's death blast deals 2d10 fire to creatures within 10 feet on a Dexterity save.",
"Transport via Plants":"Creates a temporary passage between a large, non-living plant nearby and a distant plant on the same plane that you have already seen or touched. For one round, creatures can step into one plant and emerge from the other for just 5 feet of movement.",
"Wall of Thorns":"Creates a thorny, sight-blocking barrier as a long wall or ring. Creatures in its area make a Dexterity save, taking 7d8 piercing on a failure or half on success. Crossing it quadruples movement cost, and entering or ending a turn inside requires another save for 7d8 slashing. Higher slots add 1d8 to each damage type.",
"Word of Recall":"Instantly transports you and up to five willing creatures within reach to a sanctuary you set earlier, placing them at the nearest open space to that spot. You can only establish a sanctuary by casting it at a site tied to your deity, and without one, the spell does nothing.",
"Conjure Celestial":"Summons a friendly celestial with challenge rating 4 or less that obeys your spoken orders as long as they fit its moral outlook, and defends itself without commands. Using a 9th-level slot raises the maximum challenge rating to 5.",
"Conjure Hezrou (UA)":"You summon a demon that obeys only while you pass a Charisma check at the start of each of its turns. The check's bonus depends on the food's value, and the DC rises by 2 each round. If you fail, the demon feeds on nearby corpses or attacks, and it returns to its home plane once badly hurt.",
"Dream of the Blue Veil":"You and up to eight willing creatures fall unconscious, seeing visions of another world. If six hours pass, everyone is transported to a safe spot near where a linked item was made or a linked creature was born. Damage ends it only for the injured creature, and harm to you ends it for all.",
"Mordenkainen's Magnificent Mansion":"Creates a private extradimensional mansion lasting one day, entered through a portal you place and can open or close from nearby. You design its floor plan and furnishings within a size limit, and a hundred obedient servants tend guests and provide a lavish feast.",
"Plane Shift":"Lets the caster and up to eight willing companions travel to another plane, either to a described place or a known teleportation circle. It can also send an unwilling foe to a random spot on a chosen plane: a melee spell attack must hit, and the target then makes a Charisma save to resist.",
"Teleport":"Instantly moves you and up to eight willing companions, or one object that fits in a 10-foot cube, to a known destination on your plane. A d100 roll decides the outcome based on how well you know the place: a mishap deals 3d10 force damage, and a miss scatters arrivals by a percentage of the original distance.",
"Temple of the Gods":"Conjures a temple within a cube up to 120 feet per side that lasts a day. Chosen creature types (celestials, elementals, fey, fiends, undead) must beat a Charisma save or be barred from entering, and those inside suffer a d4 penalty subtracted from their d20 rolls. Healing from spells of 1st level or higher also restores extra HP equal to the caster's Wisdom modifier (minimum 1).",
"Demiplane":"Conjure a shadowy doorway on a nearby solid surface that leads into a bare 30-foot-cube room of wood or stone. When the effect ends, the door vanishes and anything inside is stranded there. You can also link the doorway to a room you made earlier or one another caster made, if you know its contents.",
"Incendiary Cloud":"Creates a 20-foot-radius sphere of ember-streaked smoke that blocks sight and is blown away by strong winds. Creatures inside make a Dexterity save, taking 10d8 fire damage on a failure or half on success, and repeat it when entering or ending a turn there. It drifts 10 feet from the caster each turn.",
"Maze":"Banishes one visible creature into a shifting maze dimension while you concentrate, for up to ten minutes. The captive can use its action to attempt escape with a DC 20 Intelligence check, though minotaurs and goristro demons always succeed. Afterward, it returns to its former spot or the nearest open space.",
"Mighty Fortress":"Summons a stone stronghold covering 120 feet square, with four 30-foot turrets, walls, and a three-floor keep, along with a hundred invisible servants and food for a nine-course feast daily. It vanishes after seven days, but recasting it on the same spot weekly for a year makes it permanent.",
"Reality Break":"Failing a Wisdom save stops the target from taking reactions, and each turn it rolls a d10 for a chaotic effect: 6d12 psychic damage, 8d12 force damage (halved on a Dexterity save), a teleport of up to 30 feet with 10d12 force damage, or 10d12 cold damage. It can retry the Wisdom save at the end of each of its turns to end the spell.",
"Tsunami":"A towering wall of water deals 6d10 bludgeoning damage to creatures in its path, or half on a successful Strength save. Each turn it pushes 50 feet away from you, dealing 5d10 to creatures it reaches unless they pass a Strength save. Its height shrinks and its damage drops by 1d10 each round until it fades.",
"Blade of Disaster":"Conjures a blade-shaped tear in space that makes up to two melee spell attacks against nearby targets, each dealing 4d12 force damage. A roll of 18 or higher on the die is a critical hit, adding 8d12 more. As a bonus action, you can move it up to 30 feet and attack twice again. It passes through barriers, including Wall of Force.",
"Gate":"Creates a circular portal, 5 to 20 feet wide and aimed as you choose, linking to a spot on another plane for up to a minute while you concentrate. Anything entering its front is carried across, and naming a specific being can draw it through to your side, where it keeps its own will.",
"Storm of Vengeance":"A storm cloud spans a 360-foot radius around a visible point. Creatures beneath must make a Constitution save or take 2d6 thunder damage and be deafened. Each later turn you concentrate brings a new effect: 1d6 acid rain, six 10d6 lightning bolts (Dexterity save for half), 2d6 hail, then 1d6 cold damage in obscuring gusts.",
"Wish":"Wish copies any spell up to 8th level without its requirements, or produces one chosen effect: a non-magic object worth up to 25,000 gp, full healing for twenty creatures, resistance to a damage type for ten allies, eight-hour immunity to an effect, or a reroll of a recent roll. Other uses tax you and may end future casting.",
"Guidance":"Touching a willing creature lets it roll a four-sided die and add the result to one ability check of its choice, rolled either before or after the check. The boost is spent after that single use.",
"True Strike":"Studying a chosen foe reveals its weak spots. On your next turn, your opening strike against it has an edge, as long as you keep concentrating on the magic.",
"Beast Bond":"Touching a friendly or charmed beast with a mind of low intelligence creates a psychic link while you can see each other. The beast can grasp your messages and send back basic feelings. Meanwhile, it attacks with extra accuracy against foes within 5 feet of you that you can spot.",
"Comprehend Languages":"For one hour, you grasp the meaning of speech you hear and written words you see, as long as you're touching the surface they're on. Reading a full page takes roughly a minute.",
"Detect Evil and Good":"Within 30 feet, this sense reveals the presence and location of creatures from several supernatural groups, including fiends and undead. It also detects whether nearby places or objects have been sanctified or corrupted. Thick stone, metal, or dense earth can block it.",
"Detect Magic":"For up to ten minutes, you can sense magic within 30 feet of you. With an action, you can see a glow around visible magical creatures or objects and learn what kind of magic they hold. Thick stone, metal, lead, or wood can block the detection.",
"Detect Poison and Disease":"While you concentrate for up to ten minutes, you sense toxins, venomous creatures, and illnesses within 30 feet, learning each one's location and type. Thick stone, metal, lead, or wood can block this sensing.",
"Gift of Alacrity":"Touching a willing ally lets them add an extra d8 to each initiative roll they make. The bonus lasts for eight hours.",
"Guiding Hand (UA)":"Conjures a small, intangible glowing hand that leads you toward a mapped real-world landmark on your plane. It retreats as you advance and beckons you onward when you stay put. It lasts while you concentrate.",
"Hunter's Mark":"Mark a visible foe so your weapon hits deal an extra 1d6 damage to it, and you gain advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Survival checks to track it. Concentration can hold this for up to an hour, longer with higher slots, and a bonus action re-marks a new foe once the first drops.",
"Identify":"Holding one magic item or enchanted object for the whole casting reveals its abilities, how to use it, whether it needs attunement, its remaining charges, any spells affecting it, and which spell made it. Touching a creature instead reveals the spells currently affecting that creature.",
"Infallible Relay (UA)":"Targeting someone you've already talked to on the same plane, this spell rings the nearest working phone within 100 feet of them, and it fails if none is close enough. They must pass a Charisma save or pick up, and once connected, they can't end the call without succeeding on another Charisma save.",
"Sense Emotion (UA)":"Focusing your senses reveals the dominant feeling of one visible humanoid within 30 feet, and you can repeat the check as an action on later turns. Non-humanoids, or creatures immune to being charmed, always seem calm to you.",
"Speak with Animals":"For ten minutes, you can understand and talk with beasts. They can share what they've noticed around them, such as landmarks and dangerous creatures, including anything they saw within the last day. A willing beast might also do you a minor favor if the GM allows it.",
"Augury":"A divination ritual lets the caster ask an otherworldly source whether a planned action over the next half hour will go well, badly, both, or neither. The Dungeon Master picks the reading. Each extra casting before a long rest adds a growing chance of an unreliable, random answer.",
"Beast Sense":"Lets you perceive through the sight and hearing of a willing beast you touch, switching between its senses and your own at will for as long as you maintain concentration, up to an hour.",
"Borrowed Knowledge":"For the next hour, you become proficient in one skill of your choice that you weren't already trained in, drawing on the insight of ancient minds. Casting it again before then ends the effect early.",
"Detect Thoughts":"Lets you read the surface thoughts of a visible creature within 30 feet, and dig deeper with a Wisdom save that reveals its reasoning, emotions, and a dominant preoccupation. The target can end it by winning an Intelligence contest. You can also sense unseen thinking minds nearby, though stone or metal can block them.",
"Find Traps":"Reveals whether a deliberately built hazard, such as a magical ward or mechanical pit, lies within your line of sight, along with the general kind of danger it poses but not its exact position.",
"Fortune's Favor":"Lets a selected creature spend the spell to roll an extra d20 on an attack, ability check, or saving throw and keep the better result. When an attacker targets it, it can instead pick between its own die and the attacker's. Each spell slot level above 2nd adds one more target.",
"Locate Animals or Plants":"Name a kind of beast or plant to learn the direction and distance to the nearest one within 5 miles. If none are in range, you learn nothing.",
"Locate Object":"Lets you sense the direction of a familiar item, or of the nearest item of a chosen type, within 1,000 feet. Moving targets reveal where they're heading, but any lead barrier in the line between you and the object blocks the sense.",
"Mind Spike":"Target one creature you can see within range, and it makes a Wisdom save. On a failed save it takes 3d8 psychic damage, and you sense its location while you keep focus, though it can't hide from you. A success halves the damage. Each spell slot level beyond second adds 1d8 damage.",
"See Invisibility":"For an hour, you can perceive invisible creatures and objects as though they were plainly visible, and you can peer into the Ethereal Plane, where ethereal beings look faint and see-through.",
"Warp Sense":"Staying focused for up to a minute reveals gateways within 30 feet, whether or not they're active. Studying one takes an action and a DC 15 spellcasting ability check. Success reveals its destination and required key and ends the spell, while failure blocks further attempts on that gateway until you recast.",
"Clairvoyance":"You create an invisible, untouchable sensor in a familiar place or an obvious hidden spot, then perceive through it with sight or hearing as if you were there. Maintaining concentration keeps it active for up to ten minutes, and you can switch senses on your turn.",
"Tongues":"Touching a creature lets it follow any language it hears. Anyone nearby who can hear that creature and knows at least one language also grasps whatever it says.",
"Arcane Eye":"Conjures an invisible sensor that hovers for up to an hour while you concentrate, letting you see through it with normal sight and short-range darkvision. As your action, you can drift it up to 30 feet, squeezing through gaps an inch wide, but solid barriers block it and it cannot cross into other planes.",
"Divination":"The caster asks one question about an event within the next week and gets a truthful answer from the game master, perhaps a short phrase, riddle, or omen. Each extra casting before a long rest adds a 25% chance of a random, unreliable reading, rolled secretly by the GM.",
"Locate Creature":"You learn the direction to a familiar creature up to 1,000 feet away, and you can follow its movement. Alternatively, you can find the nearest creature of a kind you've seen up close, but shapeshifted targets and running water at least 10 feet wide block the effect.",
"Commune":"The caster can put up to three yes-or-no questions to a deity or divine intermediary, and each gets a truthful reply, though \"unclear\" may come back if the answer lies beyond the entity's knowledge. Each extra casting before a long rest adds a growing chance that no answer arrives.",
"Commune with City (UA)":"You merge with the surrounding city to instantly learn three facts of your choice from categories such as terrain, notable creatures, powerful otherworldly beings, electrical and signal activity, and transit lines. Your awareness reaches about a mile aboveground or 600 feet underground.",
"Commune with Nature":"Briefly merging with nature, the caster learns up to three facts about the surrounding land, reaching about 3 miles outdoors or 300 feet underground. Topics include terrain, water, local creatures and peoples, powerful otherworldly beings, planar influences, and nearby buildings, but it won't work in built-up areas.",
"Contact Other Plane":"Contact an otherworldly mind for guidance. Failing a DC 15 Intelligence save deals 6d6 psychic damage and leaves you insane until a long rest, while succeeding lets you pose up to five questions, each answered with a single word or brief phrase.",
"Legend Lore":"Naming a person, place, or object reveals a short account of its notable lore, such as popular tales, forgotten histories, or secret knowledge. Subjects of little renown yield nothing, while your prior familiarity makes the details sharper and more specific.",
"Rary's Telepathic Bond":"Up to eight willing creatures are mentally joined for an hour, letting them converse mind-to-mind in any language across any distance, though not to other planes. Beings with very low intelligence can't take part.",
"Scrying":"Target a creature on your plane with a Wisdom save, adjusted by how well you know it and your physical link to it. On a failure, an unseen sensor trails within 10 feet, letting you see and hear through it. A success blocks retries for a day.",
"Find the Path":"Reveals the quickest physical route to a familiar, fixed destination on your plane, along with its distance and direction. While you concentrate for up to a day, you instinctively take the most direct path at every fork, though not necessarily the safest one.",
"True Seeing":"For one hour, a willing creature you touch gains truesight, can spot secret doors hidden by magic, and can perceive into the Ethereal Plane, all within 120 feet.",
"Foresight":"A willing creature you touch gains a short-term glimpse of what's coming, so it can't be caught off guard, has advantage on its own rolls and saves, and enemies attacking it have disadvantage. The effect lasts 8 hours unless you cast it again first.",
"Encode Thoughts":"You turn a memory, idea, or message into a glowing, weightless strand you can carry like a ribbon, and it lasts for eight hours or until you recast the spell. While concentrating on a mind-reading effect, you can make a strand from others' thoughts instead. Holding a strand lets you take in its contents instantly.",
"Friends":"For up to a minute while you concentrate, you gain an edge on Charisma checks aimed at one creature that isn't already against you. When the magic fades, the target sees through the influence and turns hostile, possibly lashing out.",
"Mind Sliver":"This cantrip targets one visible creature with an Intelligence save. On a failed save, the target takes psychic damage starting at 1d6 and suffers a -1d4 penalty to its next saving throw before your following turn ends. The damage rises to 2d6, 3d6, and 4d6 as you gain levels.",
"Vicious Mockery":"A visible creature that can hear the caster must make a Wisdom save or take 1d4 psychic damage and have disadvantage on its next attack roll before the end of its following turn. The damage scales with character level, reaching two d4s at 5th, three at 11th, and four at 17th.",
"Animal Friendship":"This spell targets one nearby beast with Intelligence 3 or lower. Unless the beast fails a Wisdom save, it regards you as a friend for 24 hours, and harming it, or letting allies do so, ends the effect. Each higher slot adds one more beast per level above first.",
"Bane":"Up to three chosen creatures must resist a Charisma save. Each one that fails loses a d4 from every attack roll and saving throw it makes until the spell ends. Casting it with a higher slot adds one more creature per level above first.",
"Bless":"Choose up to three allies. For up to a minute, while you maintain concentration, each attack roll or saving throw they make gets a bonus from a four-sided die. Each spell slot level above first lets you choose one more creature.",
"Charm Person":"Charms one humanoid in sight unless it fails a Wisdom save, made with advantage if you or allies are fighting it. The charm lasts up to an hour and ends early if you or allies harm the target. Higher slots add one extra target per level above first, grouped within 30 feet.",
"Command":"Target one creature you can see with a one-word order. It makes a Wisdom save to resist, and if it fails, it obeys on its next turn. Undead, creatures that don't understand you, and orders that would harm them are unaffected. Each spell slot level above 1st adds one more target, all within 30 feet of each other.",
"Compelled Duel":"A creature you can see must pass a Wisdom save or be forced into a duel with you, suffering disadvantage on attacks aimed at anyone else and needing a Wisdom save to stray beyond 30 feet. The effect collapses if you attack another creature or end your turn over 30 feet from the target.",
"Dissonant Whispers":"This spell sends a painful psychic jolt that only the chosen creature can hear. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, it takes 3d6 psychic damage and must retreat with its reaction, avoiding hazards. On a success, it takes half damage and doesn't move. Deafened targets automatically succeed. Each spell slot level above 1st adds 1d6 damage.",
"Heroism":"Touching a willing ally shields them from fear and refreshes a pool of temporary hit points at the start of each of their turns, sized to your spellcasting modifier. Using a higher slot lets you bolster one more ally for each level above first. Maintaining focus keeps it going for up to a minute.",
"Hex":"Curses one creature, adding 1d6 necrotic damage to your attack hits on it and giving it disadvantage on checks with one ability you choose. Lasts up to an hour, longer with higher slots, and can jump to another creature via bonus action after the first drops to 0 hit points.",
"Id Insinuation (UA)":"A single visible creature must pass a Wisdom save or be incapacitated by warring impulses. At the end of each of its turns, it takes 1d12 psychic damage and gets another Wisdom save to shake the effect off.",
"Puppet (UA)":"Using only a gesture, you force a visible humanoid to attempt a Constitution save. On a failure, you choose the direction it must move up to its full speed, and you can also make it drop whatever it holds. Humanoids immune to being charmed are unaffected.",
"Silvery Barbs":"When a visible creature succeeds on an attack roll, ability check, or saving throw, you force it to reroll the d20 and keep the lower result. You then give advantage on another visible creature's next roll within one minute, which can be yourself, though only one such boost can be active at a time.",
"Sleep":"Roll 5d8 for a pool of hit points, then put creatures within 20 feet of a chosen point to sleep, weakest first. Undead and creatures immune to charm are skipped, and each spell slot level above first adds 2d8 to the pool. Sleepers wake if hurt or shaken.",
"Sudden Awakening (UA)":"Pick any sleeping creatures within a short distance to wake them instantly. Then, creatures lying prone in that same area can get back on their feet without spending any of their movement.",
"Tasha's Hideous Laughter":"The target must pass a Wisdom save or be knocked prone and incapacitated by uncontrollable laughter. It can retry the save at the end of each of its turns, and it gets advantage on that retry if it was triggered by taking damage. Creatures with Intelligence 4 or lower are immune.",
"Animal Messenger":"A Tiny beast you choose heads to a place you've visited and looks for a described person, then speaks your message of up to 25 words in your own voice. Flying messengers cover about 50 miles a day, and others about 25. Each spell slot level above 2nd adds 48 hours to the duration.",
"Calm Emotions":"Each humanoid in a 20-foot-radius sphere makes a Charisma save, though it may willingly fail. Those who fail either have charm or fright effects paused, or become indifferent toward chosen hostile creatures until they are attacked or harmed, or see allies hurt.",
"Crown of Madness":"A chosen humanoid you can see must fail a Wisdom save or fall under your sway, forced to make melee attacks against creatures you pick. You must spend your action each turn to keep it going, but the target can retry the Wisdom save at the end of each of its turns to break free.",
"Enthrall":"Creatures you can see that can hear you must make a Wisdom save or have disadvantage on Perception checks to notice anything besides you. Creatures immune to charm succeed automatically, and foes in combat with you or your allies get advantage on the save. The effect ends if you're incapacitated or unable to speak.",
"Gift of Gab":"As a reaction to your own speech, you pick listeners within 5 feet and erase their memory of your last six seconds of talk. They instead recall that you said the words of this casting.",
"Hold Person":"Pick one visible humanoid, which must fail a Wisdom save or be frozen in place. It can retry the save at the end of each of its turns to break free. Using a higher slot lets you affect one extra humanoid per level beyond second, as long as they are no more than 30 feet apart.",
"Jim's Glowing Coin":"A thrown coin lights up a chosen spot like a light spell, lasting about a minute. Each creature you can see within 30 feet of it that fails a Wisdom save becomes sidetracked, suffering disadvantage on Perception checks and initiative rolls.",
"Mind Thrust (UA)":"One creature makes an Intelligence save or takes 3d6 psychic damage, loses its reaction until the end of its next turn, and gets only one of movement, action, or bonus action on that turn. A success halves damage and negates the rest. Each slot above 2nd adds a target within 30 feet of the others.",
"Suggestion":"Plant a reasonable request in a listening creature. A failed Wisdom save makes it pursue that task for up to eight hours while you concentrate. Obviously harmful asks or any damage to the target end the effect, and you can tie the task to a trigger.",
"Tasha's Mind Whip":"Lash one creature with psychic force. It makes an Intelligence save, taking 3d6 psychic damage on a failure, losing its reaction until its next turn ends, and on that turn gets only a move, action, or bonus action. Success halves damage with no other effects. Each slot level above 2nd adds a target within 30 feet of each other.",
"Zone of Truth":"Creates a 15-foot sphere where creatures must make a Charisma save when they enter it or start a turn inside. Those who fail cannot knowingly speak falsehoods while inside, though they can still evade questions by staying technically truthful. The caster learns each outcome.",
"Antagonize":"A target that fails a Wisdom save takes 4d4 psychic damage and must use its reaction to attack a creature you pick. If it can't, it has disadvantage on its next attack before your next turn. A success halves the damage. Each slot level above 3rd adds 1d4 damage.",
"Catnap":"Up to three willing creatures you can see fall into a sleep-like state for ten minutes, with no saving throw. Taking damage or someone spending an action to rouse them wakes them early, but if they sleep the full time, they gain short-rest benefits and can't be affected again until a long rest.",
"Enemies Abound":"Targets must pass an Intelligence save or treat every creature they can see as an enemy for up to a minute while concentrating. Taking damage lets them retry. Their attacks and spells pick random visible targets, and they must make opportunity attacks against foes when able.",
"Fast Friends":"Charms one humanoid that sees and hears you unless it fails a Wisdom save, making it obey your requests for up to an hour while you concentrate. It can retry the save if a task harms it or clashes with its nature, with advantage when you're fighting it. Each level above 3rd adds one target.",
"Haywire (UA)":"Scrambles electronics within a 10-foot sphere, so each device randomly shuts off, stops working, works normally, or gives its user a 6d6 lightning shock on a failed Dexterity save (half on success). A creature holding a device can resist with a Wisdom save. Each spell slot level above 3rd widens the sphere by 5 feet.",
"Incite Greed":"Choose any number of creatures that can see you, and each must pass a Wisdom save or be charmed for up to a minute while you keep focus. Charmed targets can only drift toward you, and once within 5 feet they freeze, but each can retry the save at the end of its turns.",
"Motivational Speech":"Up to five nearby listeners who can hear you gain a 5-point cushion of extra health and an edge on Wisdom-based resistance rolls. When a protected ally is struck, its next attack gets an edge, and the effect ends for that ally once the cushion is gone. Each slot above 3rd adds 5 more cushion points.",
"Charm Monster":"Choose a visible creature nearby. It makes a Wisdom save, with advantage if you or allies are fighting it. On a failed save, it becomes friendly toward you for up to an hour, ending early if you or your side harms it. Each level above 4th adds a target, grouped within 30 feet.",
"Compulsion":"Creatures that can see and hear you must pass a Wisdom save or be swayed for up to a minute. Each turn, you can use a bonus action to point a sideways direction. Affected foes must spend as much movement as they can heading that way, and they may retry the save after each move to break free.",
"Confusion":"Creatures within a 10-foot sphere must make a Wisdom save or lose their reactions and act erratically, with a d10 each turn determining whether they wander, freeze, attack nearby foes, or act normally. Affected creatures can retry that save at the end of each turn. Higher slots widen the sphere by 5 feet per level above 4th.",
"Dominate Beast":"The target resists with a Wisdom save, at advantage if it's fighting you or your allies. If it fails, you can give it broad orders through a mental bond or take full control for a turn, and each instance of damage lets it retry the save to break free. Higher slots extend the duration to 10 minutes, 1 hour, or 8 hours.",
"Ego Whip (UA)":"A visible creature within reach must pass an Intelligence save or be crippled: it has disadvantage on attacks, ability checks, and saves, and cannot cast spells. The target may retry that save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.",
"Raulothim's Psychic Lance":"Targets must pass an Intelligence save or take 7d6 psychic damage and be incapacitated until your next turn. A successful save halves the damage and prevents incapacitation. Each spell slot level above the base adds 1d6 damage.",
"Synchronicity (UA)":"The touched creature shrugs off everyday hassles, as traffic lights turn green and taxis or elevators appear on cue. It moves freely through crowds, gains advantage on Stealth and vehicle-driving checks, and makes opportunity attacks against it at disadvantage. When two affected creatures' effects clash, they settle it with Charisma contests.",
"Dominate Person":"A visible humanoid must pass a Wisdom save or be charmed, with advantage if it fights you or your allies. It follows your telepathic orders, and an action grants full control. Each time it takes damage, it can retry the save to end the effect. Higher slots extend the duration: 10 minutes, 1 hour, or 8 hours.",
"Geas":"Forces a creature that understands you to make a Wisdom save or become charmed for 30 days. Each time it defies your orders, it takes 5d10 psychic damage, but only once per day. Commanding certain death ends the spell, and using a 7th or 8th-level slot extends the duration to a year.",
"Hold Monster":"Choose a visible creature and force a Wisdom save, or it stays frozen for up to a minute while you concentrate. The target can retry the save at the end of each of its turns to break free, and undead are immune. Stronger slots add one extra target per level above fifth, all within 30 feet of each other.",
"Modify Memory":"Failing a Wisdom save charms and incapacitates a visible target for up to a minute (advantage if you're fighting it). While charmed, you can erase, alter, or implant memories of events from the past 24 hours lasting 10 minutes or less. Higher slots reach 7 days, 30 days, 1 year, or any time back.",
"Synaptic Static":"Psychic energy erupts in a 20-foot sphere at a chosen point, forcing each creature there to make an Intelligence save. Creatures take 8d6 psychic damage, halved on a success, and failures are muddled for a minute, subtracting a d6 from attacks, checks, and concentration saves until an Intelligence save at the end of each turn succeeds.",
"Mass Suggestion":"Up to twelve creatures that can hear and understand you make a Wisdom save or follow a reasonable suggestion you voice, lasting up to a day. Obviously harmful requests fail outright, and hurting an affected creature ends its effect. Higher slots extend it to 10 days, 30 days, or a year and a day.",
"Otto's Irresistible Dance":"A chosen creature you can see is forced into a silly, stationary jig, unless it's immune to being charmed. While dancing, it can only shuffle in place, has disadvantage on Dexterity saves and attacks, and other creatures hit it with advantage. It can use its action to attempt a Wisdom save to break free.",
"Psychic Crush (UA)":"A creature you can see must make an Intelligence save or take 12d6 psychic damage and be stunned; success halves the damage and avoids the stun. A stunned target repeats the Intelligence save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.",
"Power Word: Pain":"Targets one visible creature with 100 or fewer hit points, slowing it to 10 feet of movement and giving it disadvantage on most rolls except Constitution saves. Casting spells requires a Constitution save or the spell is wasted. The creature can repeat that save at the end of each of its turns to end the effect.",
"Antipathy/Sympathy":"Pick a Huge-or-smaller object or creature, or a space up to a 200-foot cube, and name one kind of intelligent creature. Those creatures must pass a Wisdom save or be either repelled, becoming frightened of the target, or drawn toward it. The aura lasts 10 days, with fresh saves each day.",
"Dominate Monster":"Targets a visible creature, which must fail a Wisdom save or be charmed for up to an hour. While charmed, it can receive telepathic orders, and you can spend your action to control its every move for a turn. Advantage on the save applies if allies are fighting it. A 9th-level slot extends the duration to 8 hours.",
"Feeblemind":"A psychic blast that deals 4d6 damage to one visible creature, which must make an Intelligence save. On a failed save, its Intelligence and Charisma drop to 1, and it loses the ability to cast spells, use items, or speak coherently. Every 30 days it can retry the save, and Greater Restoration, Heal, or Wish also end the effect.",
"Power Word: Stun":"Against a visible creature with 150 hit points or fewer, this spell inflicts a stun. Creatures with more hit points are unaffected. Victims can shake it off with a Constitution save each time their turn wraps up.",
"Power Word: Kill":"A chosen creature you can see that has 100 hit points or fewer dies instantly. Anything with more hit points is unaffected.",
"Psychic Scream":"Up to ten visible foes must make an Intelligence save against this mental blast. On a failure, they take 14d6 psychic damage and are stunned, while a success halves the damage and prevents the stun. Creatures with Intelligence 2 or less are immune, and stunned victims can retry the save at the end of each turn.",
"Booming Blade":"A melee weapon strike against a nearby foe deals normal weapon damage on a hit and leaves a thunder aura until your next turn. If the target voluntarily moves 5+ feet before then, it takes 1d8 thunder damage and the aura ends. Higher levels add thunder dice to both effects at 5th, 11th, and 17th.",
"Dancing Lights":"Conjures up to four floating lights that look like torches, lanterns, or orbs, or merge into one humanoid figure, each giving dim light across a 10-foot radius. A bonus action can shift them up to 60 feet, but each must stay within 20 feet of another, and any light beyond range vanishes.",
"Eldritch Blast":"Fires force bolts, each requiring a ranged spell attack, and a hit deals 1d10 force damage. Higher levels add bolts: two at 5th, three at 11th, and four at 17th. Each bolt needs its own attack roll and can target one creature or several.",
"Fire Bolt":"Hurl a fire mote at a creature or object with a ranged spell attack. A hit deals 1d10 fire damage and can ignite an unattended flammable item. The damage rises to 2d10, 3d10, and then 4d10 at levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Frostbite":"Targeting one visible creature, this spell forces a Constitution save. On a failure, the target takes 1d6 cold damage and has disadvantage on its next weapon attack before the end of its next turn. The damage grows to 2d6, 3d6, and 4d6 at character levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Green-Flame Blade":"Strike a foe within reach with the weapon used to cast it. On a hit, green fire leaps to a second nearby creature for fire damage equal to your spellcasting modifier. Higher levels add 1d8 fire to the hit and boost both fire rolls, growing to 2d8 and 3d8 at higher tiers.",
"Hand of Radiance (UA)":"Creatures you choose that you can see in a small radius around you must make a Constitution save or take 1d6 radiant damage. The damage grows to 2d6, 3d6, and 4d6 as your character level reaches 5, 11, and 17.",
"Light":"Touch an object up to 10 feet across to make it glow in a 20-foot bright radius, with dim light reaching 20 feet beyond that, in any color you choose. If a hostile creature holds or wears the target, it can make a Dexterity save to avoid the effect.",
"Lightning Lure":"Pick one visible creature within a 15-foot radius and force a Strength save. On a failure, it's yanked up to 10 feet straight toward you, and if it ends within 5 feet, it takes 1d8 lightning damage. Damage rises to 2d8, 3d8, then 4d8 at higher character levels.",
"Ray of Frost":"Fires a chilling beam at one target using a ranged spell attack. On a hit, it deals 1d8 cold damage and slows the target by 10 feet until your next turn. The damage rises to 2d8, 3d8, and 4d8 at higher character levels.",
"Sacred Flame":"A blaze of light strikes one creature you can see. The target must dodge it with a Dexterity save or take 1d8 radiant damage, and cover doesn't help. The damage rises to 2d8, 3d8, and 4d8 as you reach levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Shocking Grasp":"A melee spell attack gives the caster advantage against targets in metal armor. A hit deals 1d8 lightning damage and stops the target from using reactions until its next turn. Damage rises to 2d8, 3d8, and 4d8 at levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Thunderclap":"Creatures other than you within a small radius must make a Constitution save or take 1d6 thunder damage. The damage rises to 2d6, 3d6, and 4d6 as your character reaches levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Word of Radiance":"Speaking a holy word unleashes searing radiance on chosen visible creatures nearby. Each target must pass a Constitution save or take 1d6 radiant damage, increasing to 2d6, 3d6, and 4d6 at 5th, 11th, and 17th level.",
"Acid Stream (UA)":"Sprays a 30-by-5-foot line of acid, forcing each creature in it to make a Dexterity save or become coated. Coated creatures take 3d4 acid damage at the start of each of their turns until someone scrapes or washes the acid off. Each spell slot level above first adds 1d4 damage.",
"Burning Hands":"A short fan of flame bursts from the caster's hands in a 15-foot cone, and each creature inside must attempt a Dexterity save. A failed save deals 3d6 fire damage, and a successful save halves it. Each spell slot level above first adds 1d6 damage.",
"Chaos Bolt":"A ranged spell attack deals 2d8 plus 1d6 damage, and your choice of one d8 sets the damage type. Matching dice make the energy leap to another creature within 30 feet, needing new attack and damage rolls, though no creature can be hit twice per cast. Each higher slot adds 1d6 damage per target.",
"Chromatic Orb":"Fire an energy sphere at a creature you can see, choosing one of six damage types. Make a ranged spell attack roll; on a hit, the target takes 3d8 damage. Each spell slot level above 1st adds another 1d8.",
"Cure Wounds":"Touching a creature restores hit points equal to an eight-sided die plus your spellcasting modifier. Undead and constructs are unaffected. Each spell slot level above first adds another eight-sided die to the healing.",
"Divine Favor":"Whenever the caster's weapon hits, it deals an extra one four-sided die of radiant damage. The benefit lasts as long as the caster keeps focusing on the spell.",
"Earth Tremor":"Shakes the ground in a 10-foot circle centered on the caster, sparing the caster. Each creature there must succeed on a Dexterity save or take 1d6 bludgeoning damage and fall prone. Loose soil or stone in the area becomes difficult terrain, and each spell slot level above 1st adds another 1d6 damage.",
"Faerie Fire":"Outlines every object in a 20-foot cube with colored light, and creatures there that fail a Dexterity save glow too. Affected targets and objects shed dim light, and attackers who can see them get advantage on attack rolls. Invisibility can't hide them.",
"Frost Fingers":"Icy blasts erupt from your fingertips in a 15-foot cone. Creatures inside must make a Constitution save, taking 2d8 cold damage on a failure or half that on a success. Casting it with a higher-level slot adds 1d8 damage for each level above first.",
"Guiding Bolt":"A ranged spell attack that hits deals 4d6 radiant damage, and the next attack roll against that foe before your next turn has advantage thanks to a glimmering glow. Each spell slot above 1st adds 1d6 damage.",
"Healing Word":"A visible creature of your choice regains hit points equal to a d4 roll plus your spellcasting modifier, but undead and constructs gain nothing. Each spell slot level above first adds one more d4 to the healing.",
"Hellish Rebuke":"Reacting to harm from a visible foe, you engulf that attacker in infernal fire. They make a Dexterity save, taking 2d10 fire damage on a failure or half on a success. Each spell slot level above first adds 1d10 damage.",
"Jim's Magic Missile":"Fires three force darts, each aimed at a visible creature with its own ranged spell attack. A hit deals 2d4 force damage, or 5d4 on a critical. Any natural 1 on an attack sends the darts back, striking you for 1 force per dart. Higher-slot casting adds a dart per level above first.",
"Magic Missile":"Conjures three bolts of force that each strike a visible target you choose, dealing 1d4+1 damage apiece. You can spread the bolts across several foes or focus them all on one. Each spell slot level above the first adds one more bolt.",
"Searing Smite":"Your next melee weapon hit before the effect ends adds 1d6 fire damage and sets the target ablaze. Each turn afterward, the target makes a Constitution save: failure means 1d6 fire damage, and success ends the effect. Casting with a higher slot adds another 1d6 to the initial hit for each level above first.",
"Tasha's Caustic Brew":"A 30-foot-long, 5-foot-wide acid stream blasts in a direction you pick. Creatures in it must pass a Dexterity save or become coated, taking 2d4 acid damage each turn until someone spends an action scrubbing it off. Each spell slot level above first adds 2d4 damage.",
"Thunderous Smite":"For the spell's duration, your first melee weapon hit adds 2d6 thunder damage, and the boom carries up to 300 feet. If the struck creature fails a Strength save, it is shoved 10 feet back and falls prone.",
"Thunderwave":"Creatures in a 15-foot cube from you must make a Constitution save or take 2d8 thunder damage and be shoved 10 feet back; a success halves the damage and prevents the shove. Loose items in the area are also pushed away, and the blast is audible 300 feet off. Each spell slot above 1st adds 1d8 damage.",
"Witch Bolt":"A ranged spell attack starts a lightning arc that deals 1d12 on a hit. While you concentrate for up to a minute, you can spend your action each turn to deal an automatic 1d12 more. Higher slots add 1d12 to the initial hit per level above first.",
"Wrathful Smite":"Your next melee weapon hit during the spell adds 1d6 psychic damage. The struck creature must succeed on a Wisdom save or become frightened of you, and it can use its action to make a Wisdom check against your save DC to shake off the fear.",
"Aganazzar's Scorcher":"Shoots a 30-foot-long, 5-foot-wide stream of flame in a direction you pick. Creatures in the path make a Dexterity save, taking 3d8 fire damage on a failure or half on a success. Casting with a higher slot adds 1d8 damage for each level above second.",
"Branding Smite":"Your next weapon hit before the spell ends deals an extra 2d6 radiant damage and glows with light, revealing the target if it's invisible. The target also emits dim light within 5 feet and can't turn invisible. Each spell slot level above 2nd adds 1d6 more radiant damage.",
"Continual Flame":"Creates a torch-bright flame on a touched object that produces no warmth and consumes no air. It can be hidden or covered but cannot be snuffed out, and it lasts until dispelled.",
"Darkness":"Creates a 15-foot-radius sphere of magical blackness at a point you select, curling around corners and defeating darkvision and ordinary light. It can travel with a held object, and an opaque cover over its source stops it. Any overlapping light from a spell of 2nd level or lower gets extinguished.",
"Flame Blade":"Summon a flaming sword in your empty hand and strike with it as an action using a melee spell attack. Hits deal 3d6 fire damage, and the blade lights the area around you. Each two spell levels above second add 1d6 damage.",
"Gust of Wind":"Unleashes a strong wind in a long, narrow line while you concentrate. Creatures starting their turn inside must make a Strength save or get pushed back, and moving toward you costs double movement. You can redirect the gust each turn as a bonus action.",
"Melf's Acid Arrow":"Fire a glowing acid arrow with a ranged spell attack. A hit deals 4d4 acid damage immediately, plus 2d4 more at the end of the target's next turn. A miss still deals half the initial damage, with no delayed harm. Each slot above 2nd adds 1d4 to both the initial and delayed damage.",
"Moonbeam":"A pillar of pale light burns anyone who enters or starts a turn inside it, forcing a Constitution save for 2d10 radiant damage, or half on success. Shapechangers roll that save at disadvantage and revert if they fail. Each slot level above 2nd adds 1d10 damage. The caster can shift the beam 60 feet each turn.",
"Prayer of Healing":"Pick up to six creatures you can see nearby to heal, each recovering 2d8 plus your spellcasting modifier. Undead and constructs gain nothing. Each spell slot level above second adds another 1d8 of healing.",
"Rime's Binding Ice":"A 30-foot cone of frost forces Constitution saves. Failures take 3d8 cold damage and are stuck with zero speed for a minute unless an action frees them. Successes take half damage and avoid the immobilizing. Each spell slot level beyond the second adds 1d8 damage.",
"Scorching Ray":"Conjures three fire bolts that you can aim at one target or split among several. Each bolt needs its own ranged spell attack roll, and a hit deals 2d6 fire damage. Each spell slot level above second adds one more bolt.",
"Shatter":"A jarring thunderous blast erupts at a spot you choose, striking everything within a 10-foot-radius sphere. Creatures there make a Constitution save, taking 3d8 thunder damage or half on success; stone, metal, and crystal beings roll at disadvantage, and loose objects in the area get hit too. Each slot level above 2nd adds 1d8 damage.",
"Snilloc's Snowball Swarm":"Magic snowballs burst at a chosen point, hitting every creature within a 5-foot-radius sphere. Each target makes a Dexterity save, taking 3d6 cold damage on a failure or half on a success. Each slot level above 2nd adds 1d6 damage.",
"Spiritual Weapon":"Conjures a floating spectral weapon that makes a melee spell attack against a creature within 5 feet, dealing 1d8 plus your casting stat modifier force damage on a hit. Using a bonus action each turn, you can move it up to 20 feet and attack again. Higher slots add 1d8 per two levels above 2nd.",
"Warding Wind":"A 10-foot-wide gale travels with you for up to 10 minutes while you concentrate. It deafens everyone inside, snuffs small exposed flames, and makes the ground hard going for others. Ranged attacks crossing it take disadvantage, and it blows away fog and gas.",
"Aura of Vitality":"While concentrating, you create a 30-foot healing zone that follows you. With a bonus action, you can restore 2d6 hit points to one creature inside it, including yourself.",
"Blinding Smite":"Your next melee weapon hit before the effect ends adds 3d8 radiant damage. The struck target must pass a Constitution save or be blinded, and it can repeat that save at the end of each of its turns to end the blindness.",
"Crusader's Mantle":"Creates a 30-foot-radius aura that follows the caster for up to a minute while they stay focused on it. Non-hostile creatures inside, including the caster, deal an extra 1d4 radiant damage on each successful weapon hit.",
"Daylight":"Creates a 60-foot-radius globe of bright light, with 60 more feet of dim light beyond it, fixed to a chosen point or moving with a held object. An opaque cover over that object blocks the glow, and the light dispels darkness from lower-level spells it overlaps.",
"Fireball":"Choose a spot within 150 feet to set off a fiery blast covering a 20-foot radius. Creatures there make a Dexterity save, taking 8d6 fire damage on a failure or half on a success. Each spell slot level above 3rd adds 1d6 damage, and no character-level scaling is listed.",
"Leomund's Tiny Hut":"You conjure a stationary, forcefield shelter about ten feet in radius around yourself, lasting hours. Up to nine mid-sized or smaller allies can join you, while other creatures, objects, and magic are kept out. You can dim or darken the interior, and the outside can be any color while staying see-through from within.",
"Lightning Bolt":"A lightning bolt tears down a long, narrow path in a direction you pick. Creatures in it make a Dexterity save, taking 8d6 lightning damage on a failure or half on a success. Loose flammable objects in the path can catch fire. Each slot level above third adds 1d6 damage.",
"Mass Healing Word":"Up to six visible creatures you choose each regain 1d4 plus your spellcasting modifier in hit points. Undead and constructs gain nothing. Each slot level above third adds another 1d4 to the healing.",
"Melf's Minute Meteors":"Six tiny orbs circle you, and each turn you can send one or two of them at targets up to 120 feet away as a bonus action. Creatures within 5 feet of an impact make a Dexterity save, taking 2d6 fire damage on a failure or half on a success. Each spell slot level above 3rd adds two more orbs.",
"Psionic Blast (UA)":"Creatures in a 30-foot cone must make a Dexterity save or take 5d8 force damage, get shoved 20 feet away, and fall prone. A successful save halves the damage and prevents the shove and prone. Each extra slot level used adds 1d8 damage.",
"Pulse Wave":"Unleashing a 30-foot cone, this spell has creatures roll Constitution saves: 6d6 force damage on a failure, half on a success. Failing creatures and loose objects are pulled 15 feet closer or shoved 15 feet away. Each slot level above 3rd adds 1d6 damage and 5 feet of movement.",
"Sending":"Lets you mentally deliver a message of up to twenty-five words to a creature you know, which can reply right away. It works across any distance, even to other planes, though cross-plane messages have a small chance of never arriving.",
"Wall of Sand":"Conjures a sand barrier up to 30 feet long, 10 feet high, and 10 feet thick that blocks sight but not movement. Creatures inside it are blinded, and each foot they move there costs three feet of movement. It lasts as long as you maintain concentration.",
"Wall of Water":"Summons a water barrier on the ground, either a straight wall up to 30 feet long and 10 feet high or a ring 20 feet across and 20 feet tall. Ranged attacks through it suffer a penalty, fire harm is cut by half, and cold effects freeze sections with 15 hit points each.",
"Wind Wall":"A gusty barrier up to 50 feet long, 15 feet high, and 1 foot thick, which you can bend into any ground-level path you like. Creatures in its area make a Strength save, taking 3d8 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. The wind keeps out gases, tiny fliers, and ordinary arrows.",
"Fire Shield":"For ten minutes, you can wrap yourself in either a fiery aura that resists cold damage or an icy one that resists fire damage. A creature that hits you with a melee attack from within 5 feet takes 2d8 damage of the matching type, and you can dismiss the effect early with an action.",
"Gravity Sinkhole":"A 20-foot-radius crushing field forms at a visible point and drags nearby creatures toward its center. Each must succeed on a Constitution save or take 5d10 force damage and be hauled to the nearest open space to the center. A success halves the damage and prevents the pull. Casting with a higher slot adds 1d10 damage per slot level above fourth.",
"Ice Storm":"Hail pounds a 20-foot-radius, 40-foot-tall column, and creatures inside make a Dexterity save. A failed save takes 2d8 bludgeoning plus 4d6 cold damage, or half that on a success, and the area stays difficult terrain until your next turn ends. Each spell slot level above fourth adds 1d8 bludgeoning damage.",
"Otiluke's Resilient Sphere":"Traps a creature or object no bigger than Large inside an impenetrable, damage-proof force globe, and unwilling targets first get a Dexterity save to avoid it. Nothing crosses the barrier, though the occupant can still breathe and can roll the sphere at half its speed. Only Disintegrate can destroy it.",
"Sickening Radiance":"Creates a 30-foot-radius zone of faint green glow that spreads around corners. Each creature that enters or starts its turn inside must make a Constitution save or take 4d10 radiant damage and gain a level of exhaustion. Glowing creatures can't benefit from invisibility. Lasts while you maintain concentration, up to 10 minutes.",
"Staggering Smite":"Your next melee weapon hit during the spell's duration deals an extra 4d6 psychic damage. The struck creature makes a Wisdom save, and on a failure it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks and loses its reactions until the end of its next turn.",
"Storm Sphere":"A 20-foot whirlwind lasts up to a minute. Creatures inside or entering it must pass a Strength save or take 2d6 bludgeoning damage. Each turn, a bonus action hurls lightning at a foe within 60 feet of the center: a ranged spell attack, with advantage against targets inside, dealing 4d6 on a hit. Each slot level above 4th adds 1d6 to every effect.",
"Vitriolic Sphere":"A glowing acid orb bursts in a 20-foot-radius blast, and each creature there makes a Dexterity save. On a failed save, it takes 10d4 acid damage plus 5d4 more at the end of its next turn. A success halves the initial damage and avoids the delayed portion. Each spell slot level above 4th adds 2d4 to the initial damage.",
"Wall of Fire":"Conjure an opaque wall of flame where one chosen face burns creatures that end a turn nearby or pass through it, for 5d8 fire damage. Creatures in its area make a Dexterity save, taking 5d8 fire on a failure or half on a success. Each spell slot level above 4th adds 1d8 damage.",
"Bigby's Hand":"Conjures a large, see-through hand of force that you direct each turn, moving it up to 60 feet to hit with a spell attack for 4d8 force damage, push or grab foes, or shield you with half cover. Each slot above 5th adds 2d8 to strikes and 2d6 to crushing.",
"Cone of Cold":"Creatures in a 60-foot cone must attempt a Constitution save, taking 8d8 cold damage on a failure or half on a success. Those reduced to zero by the chill freeze into icy statues until they thaw. Each spell slot level beyond 5th adds 1d8 damage.",
"Dawn":"Sunlight fills a 30-foot-wide, 40-foot-tall column where you choose. Creatures inside make a Constitution save, taking 4d10 radiant damage on a failure or half on a success, and again when ending a turn there. As a bonus action, you can move it up to 60 feet if you are within 60 feet of it.",
"Destructive Wave":"Choose any creatures within 30 feet to make a Constitution save. On a failure, they take 5d6 thunder plus 5d6 radiant or necrotic damage (your choice) and are knocked prone. A success halves the damage and avoids the fall.",
"Flame Strike":"Summoning a column of divine flame onto a chosen spot, this spell strikes all creatures in a 10-foot-wide, 40-foot-tall cylinder with fire and radiant damage. A Dexterity save halves the damage on success: failure deals 4d6 fire plus 4d6 radiant. Each slot level above fifth adds 1d6 to either damage type, chosen by the caster.",
"Hallow":"Creates a zone up to 60 feet across where fiends, undead, and similar otherworldly beings can't enter or use charm, fear, or possession on those inside. You can add one ongoing effect to the zone, such as fear or silence, and affected creatures can resist it with a Charisma save.",
"Holy Weapon":"Empower a weapon so its hits deal an extra 2d8 radiant damage, and it sheds light around itself. Dismissing the effect as a bonus action releases a radiant burst: creatures you can see within 30 feet make a Constitution save, taking 4d8 radiant damage and becoming blinded on a failure, or half damage without blindness on a success.",
"Immolation":"A Dexterity save halves the initial 8d6 fire damage, and failing sets the target ablaze with magic flames that ordinary means can't douse. Each turn, the burning creature retries the save, taking 4d6 fire on a failure and ending the effect on success. Creatures killed by it turn to ash.",
"Maelstrom":"Conjures a swirling pool of five-foot-deep water across a 30-foot radius that stays as difficult terrain while you concentrate. Each creature that begins its turn inside must make a Strength save or take 6d6 bludgeoning damage and be dragged 10 feet toward the center.",
"Mass Cure Wounds":"Restores hit points to as many as six chosen creatures within a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you pick. Each heals 3d8 plus your spellcasting modifier, plus an extra 1d8 for each spell slot level above 5th. Undead and constructs gain nothing.",
"Wall of Force":"Creates an invisible barrier that nothing can pass through and that ignores all damage. It can be shaped as a dome or sphere up to 10 feet in radius, or as a flat wall of up to ten 10-foot panels. Only disintegrate destroys it, and it also blocks ethereal travel while you concentrate, for up to 10 minutes.",
"Wall of Light":"Creates a glowing barrier up to 60 feet long that deals 4d8 radiant damage to creatures inside, halved on a Constitution save that also prevents blindness. Your action fires a beam at a visible foe within 60 feet; a hit deals 4d8 radiant damage and shortens the wall; damage rises 1d8 per slot above 5th.",
"Wall of Stone":"Conjures a solid stone wall of ten 10-foot panels that can span gaps or form ramps. Each panel has AC 15 and 30 hit points per inch of thickness. Creatures fully enclosed can attempt a Dexterity save to slip free, and holding concentration for the full duration makes the wall permanent.",
"Wrath of Nature":"For up to a minute, you animate nearby plants and stones in a 60-foot cube, making grass treacherous for foes. Enemies near trees risk 4d6 slashing damage via a Dexterity save each turn, while Strength saves can trap creatures in roots. Bonus-action rocks deal 3d8 bludgeoning on a spell attack hit.",
"Blade Barrier":"Conjures a spinning barrier of magical blades, either a line or a ring, that gives heavy cover to creatures behind it. Anyone who enters it or begins a turn inside must make a Dexterity save or take 6d10 slashing damage, or half on a success.",
"Chain Lightning":"A lightning bolt strikes a visible target, and three more leap to up to three other creatures or objects within 30 feet of it. Each makes a Dexterity save, taking 10d8 lightning damage on a failure or half on a success. Every slot level above 6th adds one extra leaping bolt.",
"Contingency":"You pre-load a spell that can normally target only you, and it fires automatically on you the first time a trigger you define happens. Only one such preloaded spell can be active at once, and the setup collapses if its keepsake leaves your possession.",
"Gravity Fissure":"Creates a 100-foot-long, 5-foot-wide line of gravitational force from the caster. Creatures inside it make a Constitution save, taking 8d8 force damage (half on a success). Nearby creatures within 10 feet must also save or take the same damage and be dragged into the line. Each spell slot level above 6th adds 1d8 damage.",
"Heal":"A creature you can see regains 70 hit points and is cured of blindness, deafness, and illnesses. Constructs and undead are unaffected. Each spell slot above 6th level adds 10 more healing.",
"Otiluke's Freezing Sphere":"Throwing a frigid orb at a chosen spot triggers a 60-foot-wide burst. Creatures inside make a Constitution save, taking 10d6 cold damage on a failure or half on a success. Hitting water ices a 30-foot square for a minute, and the damage rises by 1d6 per slot level above 6th.",
"Sunbeam":"Shoot a 60-foot-long, 5-foot-wide beam that forces each creature in its path to make a Constitution save. A failed save deals 6d8 radiant damage and blinds the target until your next turn, while a success halves the damage and prevents blindness. Undead and oozes roll that save at disadvantage.",
"Wall of Ice":"Summon an icy barrier as a dome, sphere, or flat panel wall. Creatures caught in its space make a Dexterity save, taking 10d6 cold damage, or half on success. Breaking a section leaves a freezing haze that deals 5d6 cold on a failed Constitution save. Each upcast level adds 2d6 and 1d6.",
"Crown of Stars":"Seven glowing orbs circle you for an hour. With a bonus action, you hurl one at a target within 120 feet using a ranged spell attack, dealing 4d12 radiant damage on a hit, and the orb is spent either way. Casting with a higher slot adds two orbs per level above 7th.",
"Delayed Blast Fireball":"A glowing bead detonates in a 20-foot-radius burst of fire when you end the spell or your concentration breaks. Creatures in the area make a Dexterity save, taking half damage on success. Base damage is 12d6, rising by 1d6 each turn the bead stays unexploded and by 1d6 per slot level above 7th.",
"Divine Word":"Creatures you can see that can hear you must make a Charisma save or suffer effects tied to their remaining hit points, ranging from deafness to instant death at 20 or fewer. Otherworldly foes such as fiends or fey that fail are sent back to their home plane for a day, regardless of hit points.",
"Fire Storm":"Conjure a fiery storm of up to ten interconnected 10-foot cubes within range, shaped as you like. Creatures in it make a Dexterity save, taking 7d10 fire damage on a failure or half on a success. It also harms objects and sets flammable items not worn or carried alight, though you may spare plants.",
"Forcecage":"Conjures an invisible force prison, either a barred cage up to 20 feet a side or a solid box up to 10 feet a side, trapping anything fully inside and pushing out creatures only partly within. Trapped creatures need a Charisma save to escape magically, and the barrier blocks ethereal travel and resists dispel magic.",
"Mordenkainen's Sword":"Conjures a hovering force-blade that makes a melee spell attack against a nearby creature, dealing 3d10 force damage on a hit. Each turn, you can use a bonus action to move the blade up to 20 feet and strike again, at the same foe or another one.",
"Prismatic Spray":"Each creature in a 60-foot cone makes a Dexterity save against one of eight randomly assigned rays. Five ray types deal 10d6 fire, acid, lightning, poison, or cold damage, halved on a success. Other rays restrain, blind, or can petrify or banish the target, and a special roll triggers two more rolls.",
"Whirlwind":"A whirlwind column, 10 feet in radius and 30 feet tall, can be steered up to 30 feet per turn. Creatures entering it make a Dexterity save, taking 10d6 bludgeoning damage (half on a success). Large or smaller creatures that fail must also pass a Strength save or be restrained.",
"Dark Star":"Creates a darkness-filled sphere of up to 40 feet in radius that crushes everything inside it. Creatures that enter it or start a turn there must make a Constitution save or take 8d10 force damage, or half on a success, and a creature knocked to 0 hit points is disintegrated.",
"Earthquake":"Shaking the ground across a 100-foot-radius area, this concentration spell turns it into difficult terrain, forces Dexterity saves to avoid prone, and can end concentration for creatures failing Constitution saves. Structures take 50 bludgeoning damage each turn, and their collapses hit creatures for 5d6 on a failed Dexterity save, half on success.",
"Maddening Darkness":"Creates a 60-foot-wide ball of magical gloom that blocks sight, even darkvision, and smothers torchlight and weaker spell light. Each creature that starts its turn inside must succeed on a Wisdom save or take 8d8 psychic damage, half as much on a success.",
"Sunburst":"Sunburst bursts brilliant light over a 60-foot radius. Creatures there make a Constitution save: on a failure they take 12d6 radiant damage and are blinded for a minute, and on a success they take half damage. Undead and oozes roll that save at disadvantage, and blinded targets can retry each turn to end the blindness. It also dispels magical darkness.",
"Telepathy":"Creates a mental bridge with a willing creature you know, letting you both instantly exchange messages, images, and sounds while on the same plane, for up to a day. Even a creature with minimal intellect can grasp what you convey.",
"Mass Heal":"Distributes up to 700 points of healing among any visible creatures nearby, in whatever split you choose. Each recipient also sheds any disease and any blindness or deafness. Undead and constructs are unaffected.",
"Meteor Swarm":"Four blazing orbs crash into chosen spots, each striking creatures in a 40-foot-radius area with a Dexterity save. Failed saves take 20d6 fire and 20d6 bludgeoning damage, or half on a success, and overlapping bursts hit a target only once. Objects in the area take damage, and unattended flammable items catch fire.",
"Power Word: Heal":"Touching a creature fully restores its hit points and ends any charmed, frightened, paralyzed, or stunned condition. A prone target can rise using its reaction. Undead and constructs are unaffected.",
"Ravenous Void":"A 20-foot gravity sphere destroys loose nonmagical objects within it and drags nearby creatures and objects inward. Creatures failing a Strength save are pulled toward it, and those entering or starting a turn inside take 5d10 force damage and are restrained, escaping with a Strength check against your save DC. Zero-HP victims are annihilated.",
"Minor Illusion":"Creates a sound or a small object-sized image, up to a 5-foot cube, that lasts one minute. Sounds can range from a whisper to a scream and imitate voices or instruments, while images can't produce light, smell, or noise. An observer can spot the trick with an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC.",
"Color Spray":"Creatures in a 15-foot cone are blinded, weakest first, drawing from a pool of 6d10 hit points that each target's current HP depletes. Creatures whose HP exceeds the remainder are spared. Unconscious or sightless creatures are skipped. Each slot level above 1st adds 2d10 to the pool.",
"Disguise Self":"Alters how you and your gear look for an hour, letting you seem a foot taller or shorter and slimmer or stouter, though your basic body shape stays the same. Anyone who studies you closely can see through it with an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC.",
"Distort Value":"This spell makes a small object seem either twice as valuable, through added ornamentation, or half as valuable, through fake dents and wear. Anyone inspecting it must succeed on an Investigation check against your spell DC to see through the deception. Each spell slot above the first allows the object to be one foot larger per side.",
"Illusory Script":"Writing becomes disguised so that only the caster and chosen companions read it as ordinary text, while others see gibberish or a false message in another hand and tongue the caster knows. Dispelling ends both the disguise and the original text, though truesight reveals the concealed message.",
"Silent Image":"Conjure a silent, visual-only likeness of a thing, creature, or phenomenon, up to a 15-foot cube. Spend your action to relocate it and animate its motion so it looks lifelike. Touching it reveals the falsehood, and an observer who studies it can unmask it with an Investigation check against your spell save DC.",
"Unearthly Chorus (UA)":"While you concentrate, a musical aura travels with you. As a bonus action, you can target one creature that sees and hears you, which makes a Charisma save. On a failure, it becomes friendly to you while the music plays and for an hour after. If you or your allies are attacking it, it succeeds automatically. You also gain advantage on Performance checks and on Deception and Persuasion checks against it.",
"Blur":"Attackers have disadvantage on their attack rolls against you while the effect lasts, since your form wavers to onlookers. Foes that sense without sight or can see through illusions ignore it.",
"Invisibility":"A touched creature, along with whatever it wears or carries, vanishes from sight for up to an hour while you maintain focus. The effect collapses early if that creature attacks or casts a spell. Using a higher-level slot lets you include one more creature for each level above the base.",
"Magic Mouth":"You plant a spoken message of up to 25 words into a visible object that no one is holding or wearing. When a trigger you choose occurs within 30 feet, a mouth appears and recites the message in your voice. The message can vanish after one delivery or keep repeating.",
"Mirror Image":"Three illusory copies of you move and mimic your actions. An attack on you may be diverted to a copy on a d20 roll of 6+ with three copies, 8+ with two, or 11+ with one. Copies have AC 10 plus your Dex modifier and are destroyed only by an attack that hits them.",
"Nathair's Mischief":"Create a 20-foot cube of whimsical, otherworldly energy that you can shift 10 feet before the first roll. Each turn, a d4 picks one of four pranks: charm, blindness, a giggling fit that incapacitates, or sticky difficult terrain. Some require Wisdom or Dexterity saves from creatures inside.",
"Nystul's Magic Aura":"Touch a willing creature or unattended object to make divination magic misread it. You can disguise its magical aura, making it look magical, mundane, or part of a chosen school, or make it seem like a different creature type or alignment. The effect lasts a day, or until dispelled if you repeat the same casting daily for 30 days.",
"Phantasmal Force":"On a failed Intelligence save, the target sees a illusion up to a 10-foot cube that only it can perceive. Each of your turns, the illusion can deal 1d6 psychic damage to the target if the illusion could plausibly harm it. The target ends the spell by passing an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your DC.",
"Shadow Blade":"Conjures a shadowy sword you can attack with, dealing 2d8 psychic damage per hit. Attacks against targets in dim light or darkness are made with advantage. Casting with higher-level slots raises the damage to 3d8, 4d8, or 5d8.",
"Silence":"A hush settles over a sphere with a 20-foot radius, blocking all sound from being made inside it or passing through it. Anything fully within gains protection from thunder damage, but creatures there are left deafened and cannot cast spells with verbal components.",
"Fear":"Creatures in a 30-foot cone must pass a Wisdom save or drop what they hold and become frightened for up to a minute. Frightened targets must sprint away each turn, and if they end a turn out of your sight, they may retry the save to end it.",
"Hypnotic Pattern":"Each creature in a 30-foot cube that sees the shifting colors makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, it is charmed, incapacitated, and its speed drops to zero. Taking damage, or another creature spending an action to rouse it, ends the effect.",
"Invisibility to Cameras (UA)":"Up to four chosen creatures nearby disappear from electronic sensors and cameras, along with whatever they wear or carry, for up to a minute while you concentrate. Ordinary sight still reveals them.",
"Major Image":"Conjures a lifelike illusion of an object, creature, or phenomenon up to a 20-foot cube, with matching sounds, smells, and temperature, though it cannot cause harm. With your action, you can move it within range and change its motion or noises. Casting it with a 6th-level or higher slot makes it last until dispelled, without concentration.",
"Phantom Steed":"Conjures a semi-solid, horse-like mount in a space you pick, with a design you choose and full tack included. You or a chosen ally can ride it for an hour at high speed. The mount vanishes if you dismiss it or it's harmed, and otherwise it slowly fades, giving the rider a minute to dismount.",
"Greater Invisibility":"You can hide yourself or a touched creature from view for up to a minute, as long as you keep concentrating, and everything they carry or wear vanishes along with them.",
"Hallucinatory Terrain":"Alters natural terrain in a 150-foot cube so it looks, sounds, and smells like another natural landscape, such as turning fields into a swamp. Built objects and creatures stay unchanged. A careful observer can make an Intelligence (Investigation) check against the spell save DC to see through it, though touch can expose it.",
"Phantasmal Killer":"A chosen creature must make a Wisdom save or become frightened. At the end of each of its turns, it repeats the save or takes 4d10 psychic damage, and one success ends the spell. Each spell slot level above 4th adds 1d10 damage.",
"Creation":"Using shadow matter, you conjure a nonliving object up to a 5-foot cube, such as wood, cloth, stone, or metal, but only in a form and substance you have seen before. It lasts from 10 minutes for gems to 1 day for plant material, and the cube grows 5 feet per slot level above 5th.",
"Dream":"Your messenger slips into a sleeping target's dreams to talk with it and reshape the scene. If the messenger appears monstrous and delivers a short message, the target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, a nightmare ruins its rest and it takes 3d6 psychic damage on waking. Possessing a piece of the target's body gives disadvantage on that save.",
"Mislead":"You turn invisible while an illusory copy of yourself appears, but the invisibility ends if you attack or cast a spell. With your action, you can move the double up to twice your speed and direct its actions, and you can perceive through it, though doing so blinds and deafens you to your own surroundings.",
"Seeming":"Alters how any number of visible creatures look, including their gear, letting you change height by a foot and make them seem lean, heavy, or average, though body shape stays fixed. Unwilling targets may resist with a Charisma save, and touch or an Investigation check can expose the disguise.",
"Mental Prison":"Targets that fail an Intelligence save take 5d10 psychic damage and become trapped in a false danger, such as fire or teeth-filled maws, that only they perceive. Escaping by moving out, attacking, or reaching through the illusion deals 10d10 psychic damage and ends it. A successful save deals 5d10 damage and ends the spell.",
"Programmed Illusion":"Creates a hidden illusion, up to a 30-foot cube, that activates on a chosen visual or audible trigger and performs for up to 5 minutes, then rests 10 minutes before it can reactivate. Creatures can expose it by touching it or with a successful Investigation check against your spell save DC.",
"Mirage Arcane":"Reshapes the look, sound, smell, and feel of terrain across an area up to a mile square, so fields can pass for swamps and roads for chasms while the land's contours stay put. Structures can be altered or created, and only truesight sees through the deception.",
"Project Image":"Create a lookalike of yourself that can appear at any remembered spot within range, ignoring barriers. You steer it as an action, moving it up to twice your speed, and see through its eyes. Harm destroys it, and a creature that inspects it can unmask it with an Investigation check against your save DC.",
"Simulacrum":"Creates a snowy, partly real duplicate of a nearby beast or humanoid with half its maximum hit points and its full stats, though it counts as a construct. It obeys your spoken commands, can be healed with costly alchemical materials, and melts away at 0 hit points.",
"Illusory Dragon":"Conjures a massive shadow dragon that frightens enemies who see it unless they pass a Wisdom save. As a bonus action, you steer it up to 60 feet and exhale a 60-foot cone forcing Intelligence saves: failures take 7d6 damage of the chosen type, and successes take half.",
"Weird":"Creatures inside a 30-foot-radius sphere that fail a Wisdom save become frightened. Each turn after that, a frightened creature rolls another Wisdom save or takes 4d10 psychic damage, and a success ends the effect for it.",
"Chill Touch":"Make a ranged spell attack against a creature for 1d8 necrotic damage on a hit, which blocks its healing until your next turn. Hitting an undead foe also gives it disadvantage on attacks against you until your following turn ends. The damage rises to 2d8, 3d8, and 4d8 as you reach levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Sapping Sting":"This spell targets one visible creature and forces a Constitution save. On a failed save, the target takes necrotic damage and is knocked prone. The damage starts at 1d4 and rises to 2d4, 3d4, and then 4d4 as the caster reaches levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Spare the Dying":"A caster's touch pulls a living creature at zero hit points back from the brink, halting its slide toward death. Undead and constructs are unaffected.",
"Toll the Dead":"Targeting one visible creature, this forces a Wisdom save, and a failure deals 1d8 necrotic damage, or 1d12 if the target is already wounded. The dice grow to two, three, and four at levels 5, 11, and 17.",
"Cause Fear":"A visible foe in range must make a Wisdom save or be gripped by dread for up to a minute, rechecking each turn to shake it off. Constructs and undead ignore it; stronger casts add one target per slot level above first, all within 30 feet of each other.",
"False Life":"Grants you a pool of temporary hit points equal to 1d4 plus 4. Each spell slot level above 1st adds 5 more temporary hit points.",
"Inflict Wounds":"Make a melee spell attack against a nearby foe. A hit deals 3d10 necrotic damage, and each spell slot level above the base adds another 1d10.",
"Ray of Sickness":"A ranged spell attack strikes one creature, and on a hit it deals 2d8 poison damage. The target then makes a Constitution save, and on a failure it stays poisoned until the end of your next turn. Each spell slot level above 1st adds another 1d8 damage.",
"Blindness/Deafness":"Choose one visible creature to make a Constitution save. On a failure, you pick whether it's blinded or deafened, for up to a minute. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns to end the effect early. Each slot level above second adds one more target.",
"Gentle Repose":"Preserves a touched corpse against decay and blocks it from becoming undead for ten days. Those days also don't count toward the time limit for resurrection spells like raise dead.",
"Ray of Enfeeblement":"A successful ranged spell attack halves the damage the target deals with Strength-based weapon attacks while the effect lasts. At the end of each of its turns, the target can attempt a Constitution save to end it.",
"Wither and Bloom":"Creatures in a 10-foot-radius sphere must make a Constitution save, taking 2d6 necrotic damage or half on a success, and plants there wilt. One chosen creature there may spend a Hit Die to heal, adding the caster's spellcasting modifier. Each slot above 2nd adds 1d6 damage and one more Hit Die.",
"Animate Dead":"Raises a nearby corpse or heap of bones as an undead servant, either a zombie or a skeleton, that you can direct with a bonus action while it stays within 60 feet. Control lasts 24 hours and can be renewed by recasting, and each slot level above 3rd lets you animate two more undead.",
"Bestow Curse":"A touched creature must make a Wisdom save or be cursed with one effect you pick: weakened ability checks, poorer attacks against you, a wasted turn each round, or an extra 1d8 necrotic damage from your attacks and spells. Concentration lasts up to a minute, and higher slots extend the duration to hours or until dispelled.",
"Feign Death":"A willing creature you touch appears dead to observers and spells that check life status, but it is blinded, incapacitated, and unable to move. It resists all damage except psychic, and any poison or disease it carries is suspended until the effect ends, which lasts up to an hour unless you dismiss it with a touch.",
"Life Transference":"The caster takes 4d8 necrotic damage that nothing can reduce, and one visible creature they choose regains twice that amount in hit points. Each spell slot above third level adds 1d8 to the damage.",
"Revivify":"A single touch brings a creature back from death if it died within the last minute, leaving it alive with just 1 hit point.",
"Speak with Dead":"For 10 minutes, this spell lets you question a non-undead corpse that still has a mouth, up to five times, using only what it knew in life. Its replies tend to be short, cryptic, or repetitive, and it may not be truthful if it sees you as an enemy.",
"Spirit Shroud":"Spirits circling you add 1d8 damage to each of your hits on foes within 10 feet, dealt as radiant, necrotic, or cold, and the target can't heal until your next turn. Chosen creatures that start their turn in that zone also lose 10 feet of speed. Each two slot levels above 3rd adds another 1d8.",
"Summon Undead":"Summons an undead spirit that fights for you for up to an hour while you concentrate. Its attacks deal 1d8 (Ghostly), 2d4 (Skeletal), or 1d6 (Putrid) damage, plus 3 and the spell's level. Each slot level above third adds 10 hit points and extra attacks.",
"Vampiric Touch":"A melee spell attack targets a creature within reach. On a hit, the target takes 3d6 necrotic damage, and you recover hit points equal to half that amount. While sustained, you can repeat the strike as an action each turn. Casting with a 4th-level or higher slot adds 1d6 damage per slot level above 3rd.",
"Blight":"Drains vitality from one visible creature nearby, which must attempt a Constitution save. Failure means 8d8 necrotic damage, and success halves it. Undead and constructs are immune, plant creatures save at disadvantage and take maximum damage, and higher slots add 1d8 per level beyond fourth.",
"Shadow of Moil":"Dark, flickering shadows cloak you, making you very hard for others to see and dimming nearby light. You shrug off radiant harm, and any creature within 10 feet that hits you takes 2d8 necrotic damage from the lashing shadows.",
"Spirit of Death":"Summons a spectral reaper for up to an hour while you concentrate; it acts after you in combat and obeys orders. Its scythe strikes with advantage for 1d8 + 3 + spell's level in necrotic damage; haunted foes may be frightened on a failed Wisdom save. Higher levels add hit points and extra scythe swings.",
"Contagion":"A melee spell attack that poisons the target on a hit. Each turn, the victim makes a Constitution save: three successes end the effect, while three failures bring a disease of the caster's choice for up to a week.",
"Danse Macabre":"Animates up to five nearby Small or Medium corpses as zombies or skeletons, each adding your spellcasting modifier to its attack and damage rolls. A bonus action lets you direct all of them at once while they stay within 60 feet. Each slot level above fifth adds two more corpses.",
"Enervation":"A dark tendril seizes a visible creature, which must make a Dexterity save. Success deals 2d8 necrotic damage and ends the spell. Failure deals 4d8, and while you concentrate, your action each turn deals 4d8 more and heals you for half that. Higher slots add 1d8 per level above 5th.",
"Negative Energy Flood":"Blasts a visible non-undead creature with negative energy, requiring a Constitution save: 5d12 necrotic damage on a failure, half on a success. A creature killed this way rises as a zombie at the start of your next turn. Targeting undead instead gives them temporary hit points equal to half of a 5d12 roll, with no save.",
"Raise Dead":"Revives a creature that has been dead for up to ten days, returning it with 1 hit point if its soul is willing, and cures poison and nonmagical illness it had at death. The revived creature takes a -4 penalty to attack rolls, saves, and ability checks, easing by 1 after each long rest.",
"Circle of Death":"Negative energy erupts in a 60-foot-radius sphere around a chosen point. Creatures in the area make a Constitution save, taking 8d6 necrotic damage on a failure or half on a success. Casting with a higher slot adds 2d6 damage for each level above sixth.",
"Create Undead":"Animates up to three slain Medium or Small humanoids as obedient ghouls, which you can direct telepathically with a bonus action while they're within 120 feet. Control lasts 24 hours and can be renewed by recasting. Higher-level casting animates more ghouls, or ghasts, wights, or mummies at the top tiers.",
"Eyebite":"Your eyes turn into a dreadful void, forcing one visible creature within 60 feet to make a Wisdom save or suffer slumber, a terrified flight from you, or weakness with attack and check penalties. Each later turn you can shift the curse to a new foe, but anyone who resisted once is immune to this casting.",
"Harm":"This spell targets one visible creature, which must make a Constitution save. On a failed save it takes 14d6 necrotic damage, or half on a success, but it can't be reduced below 1 hit point. A failed target also has its maximum hit points lowered by the damage for an hour, unless a disease-curing effect restores them sooner.",
"Magic Jar":"Your spirit leaves your body and inhabits a vessel, from which it can take over a humanoid within 100 feet that fails a Charisma save, trapping that creature's soul inside the vessel. You keep your own mental scores and class abilities in the borrowed body, and you can leave it to return home.",
"Soul Cage":"Triggered when a visible humanoid dies, this traps its soul for up to six uses: healing 2d8 HP, asking it a question, gaining advantage on one roll, or spying through a sensor for up to 10 minutes.",
"Finger of Death":"A visible creature must pass a Constitution save or take 7d8+30 necrotic damage, or half that on a success. If the blast kills a humanoid, the corpse rises at the start of your next turn as a permanently obedient undead servant.",
"Resurrection":"Restores a slain creature to full health if its spirit is willing, sealing wounds, regrowing lost limbs, and purging ordinary poisons and illnesses. The revived figure suffers a temporary penalty to rolls and checks that lessens with each long rest.",
"Tether Essence":"Two creatures you can see make Constitution saves, at disadvantage if they stand within 30 feet of each other, and either may choose to fail. If both fail, they share damage and healing for up to an hour regardless of distance, and the link ends for both when either drops to 0 hit points.",
"Abi-Dalzim's Horrid Wilting":"Draws moisture from every creature in a 30-foot cube, forcing Constitution saves. Failures take 12d8 necrotic damage and successes take half. Constructs and undead are immune, plants and water elementals roll with disadvantage, and nonmagical plants that aren't creatures die outright.",
"Clone":"Creates a dormant copy of a creature that grows to adulthood over about four months inside a sealed vessel. If the original dies and its soul is willing, the soul moves into the copy, which keeps the same mind, memories, and skills but none of the gear.",
"Astral Projection":"You and up to eight willing allies send your spirits into the Astral Plane, leaving your bodies in a deep suspended sleep. Your astral forms can roam between planes, tethered by a silver cord, until you choose to end the effect, a dispel removes it, or a drop to zero hit points ends it.",
"Time Ravage":"A creature you can see takes 10d12 necrotic damage on a failed Constitution save, or half on a success. A failed save also ages it until only 30 days remain, giving disadvantage on attacks, checks, and saves and halving its walking speed. Only Wish or Greater Restoration cast with a 9th-level slot can reverse this.",
"True Resurrection":"Returns a creature that has been dead for under 200 years, and not from old age, to life at full hit points if its soul is willing. It also heals wounds, purges poisons and diseases, lifts curses, regrows missing parts, and can conjure a new body if the original is gone, given its name.",
"Control Flames":"Target a visible nonmagical flame within a 5-foot cube to spread it 5 feet onto fuel, snuff it out, alter its light or color for an hour, or animate shapes in it for an hour. Up to three lasting effects can run at once, each dismissible as an action.",
"Druidcraft":"Choose one minor effect: a faint, harmless display that previews the next day's weather, a plant bud or blossom that opens at once, a small harmless sensation no larger than a cube, or a candle, torch, or small campfire lit or snuffed out.",
"Gust":"Gust lets you aim a puff of air at a point you can see to do one of three things: shove a creature of Medium size or smaller 5 feet unless it succeeds on a Strength save, nudge a loose object weighing up to 5 pounds 10 feet, or create a harmless wind effect like stirring foliage.",
"Magic Stone":"Enchanted pebbles can be hurled or slung by the caster or an ally as a ranged spell attack. A hit deals 1d6 plus the caster's spellcasting modifier in bludgeoning damage, and the magic is spent after one throw whether or not it connects. Casting it anew dispels any stones enchanted from the previous casting.",
"Mending":"This cantrip seals one break or rip up to a foot across in any direction, leaving no sign it was ever damaged. It can repair the physical harm to magic items and constructs, but it cannot restore lost magic.",
"Message":"Whispering toward one chosen creature, you send a private message that only it hears, and it can whisper a reply that only you catch. If you know the target well and it lies beyond a barrier, the message can pass through solid material, unless magical silence or sufficiently thick stone, metal, lead, or wood blocks it.",
"Mold Earth":"Reshapes a dirt or stone patch you can see, up to 5 feet across. You can nudge loose soil a few feet, etch lasting images for an hour, or toggle ground between difficult and normal terrain. Two lasting effects max; you can end one as an action.",
"On/Off (UA)":"This cantrip switches a nearby electronic device on or off, but only if it has an easy-to-reach external power control. Devices that need a software shutdown sequence can't be affected.",
"Prestidigitation":"Lets the caster perform minor utility tricks, such as a harmless sensory flourish, lighting or snuffing a small flame, cleaning or soiling a tiny object, or flavoring a small amount of inanimate matter. Up to three lasting effects can persist at once, and each can be ended with an action.",
"Primal Savagery":"Make a melee spell attack against a creature within reach to deal acid damage on a hit. The damage starts at 1d10 and rises to 2d10, 3d10, and 4d10 at higher character levels.",
"Shape Water":"You can sway a visible volume of water up to a five-foot cube, pushing its flow up to five feet, shaping it into animated forms, recoloring or clouding it, or freezing it for an hour if no creature is inside. Only two of these lasting effects can run at once.",
"Shillelagh":"Imbues a club or quarterstaff you hold with natural power, letting melee strikes with it use your spellcasting ability instead of Strength for attack and damage rolls. The weapon's damage die becomes a d8, and it counts as magical for the duration.",
"Thaumaturgy":"Conjures harmless, showy effects nearby: briefly amplifying your voice, altering flames, rumbling the ground, producing a sound from a chosen spot, or snapping a door or window open or shut. Repeated casts can keep up to three lasting effects running, each ended with an action.",
"Thorn Whip":"A thorny vine lashes out at a distant foe and requires a melee spell attack roll. On a hit, it deals 1d6 piercing damage and can haul a Large or smaller creature up to 10 feet closer. The damage rises to 2d6, 3d6, and then 4d6 as the caster gains levels.",
"Arcane Weapon (UA)":"Channeling magic into a weapon you hold adds 1d6 damage on each hit, in a type you choose from several energy or toxic options. A bonus action lets you switch that type. Casting it with a 3rd-level or higher slot extends concentration to eight hours.",
"Catapult":"Hurls an unworn object of up to 5 pounds up to 90 feet in a chosen direction. A creature in its path can dodge it with a Dexterity save; otherwise it is struck and the object stops. Impact deals 3d8 bludgeoning damage to both object and target. Higher slots add 5 pounds and 1d8 damage.",
"Create or Destroy Water":"Conjures up to ten gallons of fresh water into an open vessel, or summons a rain shower over a 30-foot cube that douses exposed flames. Alternatively, it destroys up to ten gallons of water in a container or clears fog in that same cube. Each spell slot level above first adds ten gallons or five feet to the cube's width.",
"Expeditious Retreat":"This spell lets you cover much more ground. Each turn, you can spend a quick bonus action to take the Dash action and move extra distance.",
"Feather Fall":"Up to five falling creatures have their descent slowed to 60 feet per round for up to a minute. Any that reach the ground before then take no fall damage and land on their feet.",
"Goodberry":"Conjures up to ten magical berries into your palm. Any creature can use its action to eat one, regaining 1 hit point and gaining a full day's sustenance, but the berries lose their magic if they go uneaten for a day.",
"Jump":"Touching a creature triples how far it can jump for up to one minute.",
"Longstrider":"Raises one touched creature's speed by 10 feet for the spell's duration. Each spell slot level above 1st lets you affect one more creature.",
"Magnify Gravity":"Creatures in a 10-foot-radius sphere make a Constitution save, taking 2d8 force damage and losing half their speed until their next turn ends on a failure. Success halves the damage. Loose objects there need a Strength check to move until your next turn, and each slot above 1st adds 1d8 damage.",
"Purify Food and Drink":"Cleanses ordinary, non-magical food and drink within a 5-foot-radius globe, placed wherever you choose, leaving them free of toxins and disease-causing contaminants.",
"Remote Access (UA)":"For ten minutes, you can operate one nearby electronic gadget as though holding it, limited to the controls a person could reach by hand. The magic simulates the device's inner workings electronically instead of physically moving it.",
"Wild Cunning (UA)":"Invoking nature spirits, the caster picks one of six aids: locating nearby tracks (granting advantage on tracking checks for an hour), finding food, fresh water, or shelter, or having spirits set up or tear down a camp.",
"Zephyr Strike":"Your movement during the spell provokes no opportunity attacks. Once, before it ends, you can gain advantage on one weapon attack on your turn, adding 1d8 force damage on a hit. Hit or miss, your walking speed rises by 30 feet until that turn ends.",
"Alter Self":"Lasting up to an hour while you concentrate, this spell lets you pick one transformation: underwater breathing with a swimming speed, a disguise that leaves your stats unchanged, or magical natural weapons whose unarmed strikes deal 1d6 damage with a +1 bonus. You can switch to another option with an action.",
"Arcane Hacking (UA)":"Concentrating for up to an hour, you get advantage on Intelligence checks using hacking tools to crack software encryption on a foreign system. Such checks can also beat protective spells of 2nd level or lower, using the caster's spell save DC. A 3rd-level-or-higher slot lets you counter guarding spells up to that slot's level.",
"Barkskin":"A willing creature you touch gets tough, bark-like skin that lasts while you keep concentrating. Its armor class can't drop below 16, whatever armor it wears.",
"Cordon of Arrows":"Four planted projectiles guard an area. Whenever a creature other than you enters or ends its turn within 30 feet, one flies at it, forcing a Dexterity save or dealing 1d6 piercing damage before being destroyed. Casting with a higher slot adds two more projectiles per level above second.",
"Darkvision":"Grants a willing ally the ability to see in darkness out to 60 feet for eight hours.",
"Dragon's Breath":"A willing creature with a mouth can exhale a 15-foot cone of acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison, chosen when cast. Those caught in it make a Dexterity save, taking 3d6 damage on a failure or half on a success. Casting with a higher slot adds 1d6 damage per slot level above second.",
"Earthbind":"A creature you can see must make a Strength save or lose its flying ability for up to a minute while you concentrate. Any creature already airborne falls at 60 feet per round until it reaches the ground or the effect ends.",
"Enhance Ability":"Grants a touched creature one of six boons for up to an hour, as long as you keep concentrating. Each gives advantage on one ability's checks. Bear's Endurance also adds 2d6 temporary hit points, and Cat's Grace prevents fall damage up to 20 feet. Each slot level above second adds one more target.",
"Enlarge/Reduce":"Changes the size of a visible creature or an unworn, unheld object for up to a minute. An unwilling creature can resist with a Constitution save. Enlarge doubles size and grants advantage on Strength checks and saves plus 1d4 extra weapon damage. Reduce halves size and imposes disadvantage plus 1d4 less weapon damage.",
"Heat Metal":"Heats a metal item you can see, like a weapon or armor, dealing 2d8 fire damage to anything touching it. While you concentrate, you can reheat it each turn as a bonus action. Those holding or wearing it must make a Constitution save or drop it. Higher slots add 1d8 per level above 2nd.",
"Immovable Object":"Touching an object of 10 lb or less pins it in place, though chosen creatures can still move it. Airborne objects hold up to 4,000 lb, and a creature may shift one 10 feet via a Strength check against your save DC. Higher slots boost the DC, weight cap, and duration.",
"Kinetic Jaunt":"For up to a minute while concentrating, you move 10 feet faster, avoid triggering opportunity attacks, and can pass through other creatures without their space counting as difficult terrain. If you end a turn sharing a space with a creature, you're pushed back to your last free square and take 1d8 force damage.",
"Knock":"Pick a visible door, chest, padlock, or similar object, and one of its locks, bars, or jams gives way. If it is sealed by an Arcane Lock, that effect is paused for 10 minutes. A booming knock can be heard up to 300 feet away.",
"Levitate":"Lifts one visible creature or loose object up to 500 pounds, keeping it aloft for up to ten minutes while you concentrate. An unwilling creature can dodge it with a Constitution save. Lifted targets can be raised or lowered 20 feet per turn and drift gently down when it ends.",
"Magic Weapon":"Turns a plain weapon you touch into one with a bonus to both attack and damage rolls, starting at +1. Spending a 4th-level slot or higher raises the bonus to +2, and a 6th-level slot or higher raises it to +3.",
"Maximilian's Earthen Grasp":"A hand of packed earth seizes a creature within five feet of it, forcing a Strength save. A failed save means 2d6 bludgeoning damage and restraint. Later, you can crush the held foe with another Strength save, taking 2d6 damage on a failure or half on a success.",
"Pyrotechnics":"Snuff out a visible flame, then either burst it into a colorful flash that forces creatures within 10 feet to pass a Constitution save or be blinded until the end of your next turn, or release a 20-foot-radius cloud of thick smoke that heavily obscures the area for up to a minute.",
"Rope Trick":"Lifts a rope upright, creating a hidden extradimensional pocket at its top that can hold up to eight creatures of Medium size or smaller. Those inside can see outward, but nothing physical or magical can pass through the entrance, and occupants are expelled when the effect ends.",
"Skywrite":"Writes up to ten words of cloud-like text across a sky you can see, lasting up to a day while you maintain concentration. Strong gusts can scatter the clouds and end it early.",
"Spider Climb":"A willing creature you touch can climb walls and crawl across ceilings while keeping its hands free. It also gets a climbing speed equal to its walking speed. The effect lasts up to an hour, as long as you maintain concentration.",
"Spike Growth":"Across a 20-foot-radius zone, the ground sprouts concealed spikes that turn it into difficult terrain. Each 5 feet a creature travels through it takes 2d4 piercing damage, and creatures that can't see the area can detect the danger with a Wisdom check against the caster's save DC.",
"Ashardalon's Stride":"Fire erupts from your feet, raising your speed by 20 feet and preventing opportunity attacks when you move. Each creature or unattended object you pass within 5 feet takes 1d6 fire damage, once per turn. Higher-level casting adds 5 feet of speed and another 1d6 fire damage per slot level above 3rd.",
"Blink":"At the end of each of your turns, you roll a d20; on 11 or higher, you slip into the Ethereal Plane and reappear nearby when your next turn begins. There you see the dim, grayed-out version of your origin plane, but you can only interact with ethereal creatures. You can end it early as an action.",
"Elemental Weapon":"Touching a plain weapon makes it magical, and you pick acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder as its damage type. Hits gain +1 to attack rolls and deal an extra 1d4 of that damage. Higher slots raise this to +2 and 2d4 at 5th or 6th level, or +3 and 3d4 at 7th or above.",
"Erupting Earth":"A chosen visible point in range erupts into a 20-foot cube of upheaved soil and rock. Creatures inside make a Dexterity save, taking 3d12 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. The area becomes difficult terrain, and each slot level above 3rd adds 1d12 damage.",
"Flame Arrows":"Enchanting a quiver makes each arrow or bolt drawn from it deal an extra 1d6 fire damage when a ranged weapon attack hits. The magic on each piece is spent after one shot, and the effect ends once twelve have been drawn. Casting it with a higher-level slot empowers two more pieces per slot level above 3rd.",
"Flame Stride (UA)":"Your speed rises by 20 feet, and moving no longer provokes opportunity attacks. Each creature or unattended object you pass within 5 feet of takes 1d6 fire damage, once per turn per target. Stronger casting adds 5 feet of speed and another 1d6 fire damage for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Fly":"A willing creature you touch can fly at 60 feet per turn while you keep concentrating, for up to ten minutes. When the magic ends, any creature still in the air plummets unless it can halt its descent. Casting with a higher-level slot lets you affect one more creature for each level above third.",
"Gaseous Form":"A willing creature turns into a drifting vapor for up to an hour while concentrating. It moves only by slow flight, takes reduced harm from ordinary physical attacks, and gets an edge on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saves. It can squeeze through tiny cracks but cannot speak, fight, or cast spells.",
"Haste":"A willing creature you can see gains double speed, +2 to Armor Class, and advantage on Dexterity saves, plus one extra limited action per turn: a single weapon attack, Dash, Disengage, Hide, or using an object. When it ends, the creature is sluggish and cannot move or act until after its next turn.",
"Lightning Arrow":"Your next ranged weapon attack becomes lightning, dealing 4d8 on a hit or half on a miss. Creatures within 10 feet of the target make a Dexterity save, taking 2d8 on a failure or half on success. Each slot level above 3rd adds 1d8 to both effects.",
"Meld into Stone":"You fuse your body and gear into a stone large enough to hold you for 8 hours, becoming undetectable and unable to see or move except to exit where you entered. Partly breaking or reshaping the stone ejects you and deals 6d6 bludgeoning damage, while destroying it completely deals 50.",
"Plant Growth":"Within a 100-foot circle, ordinary plants turn dense and tangled, so creatures moving through pay four feet of movement per foot, though you can leave chosen spots unaffected. Alternatively, you can enrich plants across a half-mile circle for a year, doubling their harvest.",
"Slow":"Up to six creatures in a 40-foot cube must pass a Wisdom save or be hampered: their speed is halved, they take -2 to AC and Dexterity saves, they lose reactions, and they get only one action or bonus action per turn. Affected creatures retry the save each turn to end it. No damage is dealt.",
"Speak with Plants":"Plants in a 30-foot radius gain limited awareness, letting you question them about the past day's events and creatures that passed. You can either clear overgrowth into open ground or turn plant-covered ground into hindering difficult terrain for 10 minutes. Plant creatures can be conversed with, though you gain no control over them.",
"Tiny Servant":"Turns a small, unattached, nonmagical object you touch into a creature with 10 HP and AC 15 that you can direct for 8 hours or until it drops to 0 HP. Its slam deals 1d4+3 bludgeoning damage. Upcasting adds two more animated objects for each level beyond 3rd.",
"Water Breathing":"Up to ten consenting creatures you can see can breathe while submerged for a full day, and they keep their normal ability to breathe air.",
"Water Walk":"Up to ten willing companions you can see can walk across water, mud, snow, lava, and similar surfaces as if they were solid ground, though lava still burns. A creature submerged beneath a liquid is lifted to the surface at 60 feet per round.",
"Control Water":"You manipulate freestanding water within a cube up to 100 feet wide, raising its level, splitting it into a trench, steering its currents, or forming a vortex. The whirlpool forces Strength saves, dealing 2d8 bludgeoning damage on a failed save and half on a success, and it pulls nearby creatures inward.",
"Elemental Bane":"Choose a visible creature and a damage type: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder. On a failed Constitution save, the target takes an extra 2d6 of that type the first time each turn it's hit by it, and loses resistance to that type. Each slot above 4th adds another target within 30 feet of the others.",
"Fabricate":"Turns gathered raw materials you can see into finished goods of the same substance, up to a 10-foot cube in size. Metal, stone, and other minerals are limited to a single 5-foot cube, and creatures and magic items can't be made, while intricate crafted goods require tool proficiency.",
"Giant Insect":"You turn up to ten centipedes, three spiders, five wasps, or one scorpion into oversized versions that obey your spoken commands while you concentrate. Each lasts until it drops to 0 hit points or you spend an action ending its change. Your DM might allow similar swaps of beasts.",
"Guardian of Nature":"You pick a feral beast or barky tree shape. Beast form adds 10 feet of speed, 120-foot night vision, advantage on Strength attacks, and 1d6 force on melee hits. Tree form grants 10 temporary HP, advantage on Constitution saves and Dexterity/Wisdom attacks, and makes nearby ground difficult for foes within 15 feet while grounded.",
"Polymorph":"A creature you can see is turned into a beast with a challenge rating no higher than its own, taking on that beast's stats and hit points. Unwilling targets get a Wisdom save, but shapechangers always succeed. If the target drops to zero in beast form, it returns to its original body, and leftover damage carries over to that body.",
"Stone Shape":"Touch a stone object up to Medium size, or a stone section no more than 5 feet across, and reshape it into nearly any form, such as a weapon, idol, box, or a passage through a thin wall. You can also shape a stone door so it seals shut.",
"System Backdoor (UA)":"Grants covert administrator control over any computer system not enhanced by technomagic, overriding technomagic effects up to 3rd level. When the effect ends, the access disappears, though activity logs remain untraceable to you. Using a 5th-level or higher slot extends this to technomagic effects up to that slot's level.",
"Animate Objects":"Turns up to ten unattended, nonmagical objects into constructs you control, with larger items using more of that limit. Each has size-based AC, hit points, and slam attacks dealing 1d4+4 to 2d12+4 damage. You can direct them as a bonus action within 500 feet, and higher slots add two more objects per level above fifth.",
"Awaken":"Transforms a huge-or-smaller beast or plant with little to no intelligence into a creature with Intelligence 10 that speaks one of your languages. Awakened plants also gain movement and senses. The creature stays charmed by you for 30 days, then its attitude depends on how you treated it.",
"Control Winds":"You seize control of the air in a large cube within sight, choosing a steady gust that can hinder ranged attacks and slow upwind travel, a downward blast that forces flyers to make a Strength save or fall prone, or a rising current that softens falls and boosts jumps.",
"Create Spelljamming Helm":"Touching an empty chair no bigger than Large turns it into a Spelljamming Helm, a seat that lets its occupant pilot spelljamming ships.",
"Passwall":"Opens a temporary passage up to 5 feet wide, 8 feet tall, and 20 feet deep through a visible wooden, plaster, or stone surface, lasting one hour. When it closes, anything inside is pushed to the nearest free space at that surface, and the surrounding structure stays sound.",
"Reincarnate":"Touching a dead humanoid, or a piece of one, that died no more than ten days ago builds a new adult body and pulls the spirit back, but only if the spirit is free and willing. The DM rolls on a table or picks the new race, and the creature keeps its memories and abilities.",
"Shutdown (UA)":"Devices nearby that no creature is holding or directly controlling shut off. A creature actively using one can resist with a Constitution save. Until the effect ends, devices can't be started or restarted.",
"Skill Empowerment":"Touch a willing ally to let them double their proficiency bonus on ability checks for one skill they already know. You must maintain focus, and the skill can't already have a doubling effect like Expertise.",
"Swift Quiver":"Your quiver becomes an endless source of ordinary arrows or bolts that appear in your hand when you reach for them. Each turn, you can use a bonus action to fire two shots from a ranged weapon that draws on it, and the conjured ammunition vanishes when the effect ends.",
"Telekinesis":"Through pure concentration, you can drag a creature up to Huge size 30 feet by winning a contest of your spellcasting check against its Strength, leaving it restrained until the end of your next turn. Loose objects weighing up to 1,000 pounds slide 30 feet automatically, while items held by a creature require a similar contest.",
"Temporal Shunt":"Triggered when a visible creature attacks or starts a spell, the target must pass a Wisdom save or be hurled out of time, nullifying that action. It returns at the start of its next turn, unaware of what happened. Each slot above 5th adds one more target, all within 30 feet of each other.",
"Transmute Rock":"Reshape a visible stone or mud patch within a 40-foot cube. Rock can become sludge that slows movement and traps creatures (Strength save), or fall from a ceiling for 4d8 bludgeoning damage (Dexterity save, half on success). Shallow mud can instead harden into stone, restraining creatures caught inside on a failed Dexterity save.",
"Bones of the Earth":"Conjures up to six 5-foot-wide stone pillars, each with AC 5 and 30 HP, rising from visible ground. A creature on a rising pillar makes a Dexterity save or is lifted, and a pillar blocked by a ceiling deals 6d6 bludgeoning damage and pins its rider. Each slot above 6th adds two pillars.",
"Create Homunculus":"You cut yourself for 2d4 piercing damage that nothing can reduce, then bind your blood and materials into a loyal homunculus companion that dies if you do. After long rests, you can spend Hit Dice to shift some of your maximum HP onto it, adding your Constitution modifier to each roll.",
"Disintegrate":"Hurl a narrow emerald beam at a visible foe. A creature that fails a Dexterity save takes 10d6 + 40 force damage and is turned to dust if this drops it to zero hit points. Huge objects lose only a 10-foot cube, and each slot above sixth adds 3d6 damage.",
"Flesh to Stone":"A Constitution save is forced on a visible target made of flesh. Failing leaves it restrained as its body starts to harden. Each turn it repeats the save: three successes end the spell, while three failures petrify it, lasting until the effect is removed if concentration holds for the full minute.",
"Investiture of Flame":"You wreath yourself in flame that makes you immune to fire and resistant to cold. Creatures that move within 5 feet of you, or end their turn there, take 1d10 fire damage. As an action, you can unleash a 15-by-5-foot fire line, where creatures make a Dex save, taking 4d8 fire damage or half on a success.",
"Investiture of Ice":"Frost coats you, granting cold immunity, fire resistance, and freedom from ice and snow movement penalties. Foes near your icy ring struggle for footing, and your action unleashes a 15-foot cone of freezing wind: failed Constitution saves deal 4d6 cold damage and halve speed, while successful saves halve the damage.",
"Investiture of Stone":"Stone shards cling to you while you concentrate, giving resistance to nonmagical physical weapon damage. Your action can cause a 15-foot-radius tremor; creatures on the ground there must succeed on a Dexterity save or be knocked prone. You can travel through earth and stone, but stopping inside it ejects you and stuns you.",
"Investiture of Wind":"Gusts encircle you, giving ranged attackers disadvantage against you and granting a 60-foot flying speed. As an action, you can conjure a 15-foot wind cube within 60 feet. Creatures inside make a Constitution save, taking 2d10 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success, and Large or smaller failures are pushed 10 feet away.",
"Move Earth":"Sculpt soil, sand, or clay within a 40-foot area by raising or lowering the ground, digging trenches, or forming walls and pillars, capped at half the area's largest side. Changes take ten minutes, and the spell involves no saving throw, attack roll, or damage dice.",
"Otherworldly Form (UA)":"Pick the Lower or Upper Planes for immunity to fire and poison or to radiant and necrotic damage, plus protection from poisoned or charmed. You also grow flying wings, gain +2 AC, use your spellcasting modifier for weapon attacks, and attack twice on the Attack action.",
"Tasha's Otherworldly Guise":"Choose the Lower or Upper Planes for a boost: you become immune to two damage types or one condition, sprout spectral wings for 40-foot flight, gain +2 AC, and make weapon attacks as magical using your spellcasting modifier. You also get a second attack when you take the Attack action.",
"Tenser's Transformation":"For up to ten minutes, you can't cast spells but gain 50 temporary hit points, advantage on weapon attacks, an extra 2d12 force damage on each weapon hit, and two attacks per Attack action. When it ends, a DC 15 Constitution save prevents one level of exhaustion.",
"Wind Walk":"The caster and up to ten willing creatures become wispy clouds for eight hours, gaining a 300-foot flying speed and resistance to nonmagical weapon damage. In cloud form they can only Dash or change back, and changing back leaves them incapacitated for a minute.",
"Create Magen":"Turns a doll you prepare into a magen of your chosen type that carries out your instructions faithfully. Making it permanently cuts your maximum hit points by the magen's challenge rating (at least 1), and only Wish can restore them.",
"Draconic Transformation":"You gain draconic senses that reveal nearby invisible creatures unless they hide, plus insubstantial wings for a 60-foot flying speed. You can also exhale a 60-foot cone that forces Dexterity saves, dealing 6d8 force damage, or half on a success.",
"Etherealness":"Lets you drift into the edge of the Ethereal Plane, passing through solid objects on your home plane while creatures there can't sense you. Climbing or descending doubles the cost of movement, and you can end the effect at will. Each slot level above 7th lets you bring up to three willing creatures within 10 feet.",
"Regenerate":"Touching a creature restores 4d8 plus 15 hit points at once, then heals it for 1 more point at the start of each of its turns for an hour. Severed limbs grow back after two minutes, or reattach instantly if the missing piece is held against the stump.",
"Reverse Gravity":"Reverses gravity in a tall cylinder, sending unanchored creatures and loose objects hurtling upward. A Dexterity save lets a creature grab a reachable fixed object and avoid the fall. Things striking a ceiling suffer a normal fall's impact, while those reaching the top hover until the effect ends and then drop.",
"Sequester":"A willing creature or object turns invisible and is shielded from divination magic and scrying sensors. A creature also enters suspended animation, where time no longer affects it. The effect ends early if a chosen trigger occurs within a mile of the target or if the target takes harm.",
"Animal Shapes":"Willing creatures you can see are transformed into beasts of challenge rating 4 or lower, and you can reshape them into new forms on later turns. Each target keeps its alignment and mental traits, but loses speech and spellcasting and can't use its gear.",
"Control Weather":"Over up to 8 hours of concentration, you shift the weather within a 5-mile circle around you, moving precipitation, temperature, or wind one step at a time. Each change takes 10 to 40 minutes to arrive, and afterward the weather slowly drifts back to normal.",
"Glibness":"For the next hour, any Charisma check you make can use a flat 15 in place of your die roll. Truth-detecting magic will also read whatever you say as honest, even when it isn't.",
"Mass Polymorph":"Concentration spell that turns up to ten visible creatures into beasts of your choosing, each with a challenge rating no higher than their own. Unwilling targets make a Wisdom save, though shapechangers always pass, and each gained beast's worth of temporary hit points lets it keep its new form until those run out.",
"Shapechange":"You can take the shape of a creature you've seen, as long as its challenge rating doesn't exceed your level and it isn't a construct or undead. You gain its physical statistics and hit points while keeping your alignment and mental scores, and you can switch forms with an action.",
"Time Stop":"Stops time for everyone except the caster, who gets 1d4 + 1 consecutive turns to act normally. The effect collapses if the caster affects another creature or someone else's belongings, or moves more than 1,000 feet from the casting spot.",
"True Polymorph":"Target a visible creature or object and reshape it. A creature can become another creature with a challenge rating no higher than its own, or an object. An object can become a friendly creature of CR 9 or less. Unwilling creatures may resist with a Wisdom save. Maintaining concentration for the whole hour makes the change permanent."};
